{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition","id":1353351,"title":"Hunters Entertainment with Paradox to create Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th edition.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-07T08:07:37-08:00","id":1353351,"title":"Hunters Entertainment with Paradox to create Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th edition.","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/Hunters_Ent/status/1203330056333844480?s=19\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/ext_tw_video_thumb/1203329159155478528/pu/img/3G-f15iOeQDfrwHP?format=webp&amp;name=large\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/Hunters_Ent/status/1203330056333844480?s=19\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunters Entertainment (@Hunters_Ent) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://mobile.twitter.com/Hunters_Ent/status/1203330056333844480?s=19\" target=\"_blank\"> https://mobile.twitter.com/Hunters_Ent/status/1203330056333844480?s=19 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> We are excited and proud to announce our partnership with @PdxInteractive to publish and develop Werewolf: The Apocalypse 5th Edition through @PlayRenegade. Release date set for 2021. Learn more: https://t.co/w5etpzyuIZ </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T08:22:07-08:00","id":1353358,"title":"","content":"Good news! I have good feelings about this edition, I think that WTA was more in need of a complete rework than any other line of WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T11:10:02-08:00","id":1353388,"title":"","content":"I cannot wait to see how W5 follows through on the mood and theme promised by this trailer (and by older announcements from White Wolf's current owners, which were consistent with this.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T12:19:21-08:00","id":1353397,"title":"","content":"I'm concerned. Wasnt a fan of V5, and 20th anniversary/4e was great. Im skeptical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T13:14:26-08:00","id":1353412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353397#post1353397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned. Wasnt a fan of V5, and 20th anniversary/4e was great. Im skeptical.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it was the mechanics of V5 that is what you don\u2019t like, then it is probably a safe assumption to think you won\u2019t like W5 since they have already announced that it will use similar mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T14:12:20-08:00","id":1353426,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty mixed on this.<br /> <br /> Hunters is a decent company, but they're more publishers than designers. They tapped Renegade Game Studio for the design... which makes sense for Hunters to do, but I'm really wondering how this pitch happened.<br /> <br /> Renegade has a lot of really strong designers, but they're not dedicated RPG folks (which can be a positive and a negative). Who's going to be working on it? Why were they picked for it? Is W5 going to end up furthering the narratives of, &quot;this is just one narrow vision of what WtA used to be,&quot; or, &quot;this is a decent werewolf game, but it's not a WtA game,&quot; by giving this to a bunch of talented people that don't have a lot of WoD experience?<br /> <br /> Like, if I heard through the grapevine that Doug Levandowski was working on a werewolf game that, like WtA, was going to explore werewolves that are more of a distinct creature instead of humans cursed during the full moon? I'd be excited. I love his work, and I'd love to see what he'd do with it. But he's pretty far from the first person I'd think of to head up a new edition of WtA. I don't know if he's on it, but Kids on Bikes is how I learned more about Renegade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T16:54:40-08:00","id":1353451,"title":"","content":"There's some language in there that sounds reminiscent of BNS metaplot/retcon crap....plus It's using the V5 mechanics...at least we still have good stuff coming out for WtA 1st-20th on SV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T08:33:20-08:00","id":1353551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353412#post1353412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was the mechanics of V5 that is what you don\u2019t like, then it is probably a safe assumption to think you won\u2019t like W5 since they have already announced that it will use similar mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one displeased with V5 is complaing about the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T09:01:31-08:00","id":1353560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353551#post1353551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one displeased with V5 is complaing about the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's true, since there's a V5 thread with a mechanics argument in the Vampire forum right this moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:11:00-08:00","id":1353611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353397#post1353397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm concerned. Wasnt a fan of V5, and 20th anniversary/4e was great. Im skeptical.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Honestly, these news left me cold. V5 and the new WW's vision/direction is just so not my WoD and taking into account the many problems I have with V5 not just on the fluff, but on the rules level too... I just can't imagine this will be any different. Or Mage, or Changeling for that matter.<br /> <br /> At best, it'll have rules concepts and/or story ideas I can tweak and use for my version.<br /> <br /> Also, I just can't imagine it'll go down without even more political controversies than V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:37:02-08:00","id":1353623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353551#post1353551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one displeased with V5 is complaing about the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do, quite vociferously. Not all the mechanics, there are plenty of smart decisions for improving on the old system there, but I can't think of a single V5 system (as in the interaction of multiple individual mechanics) that I wouldn't want to house rule on some level if I had to run the system. And I include the core dice-rolling one on that (though it's a pretty simple house rule).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T13:52:20-08:00","id":1353628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353551#post1353551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one displeased with V5 is complaing about the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The post directly above yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T17:09:49-08:00","id":1353659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353551#post1353551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one displeased with V5 is complaing about the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loathed the mechanics half as much as the fluff, but loathed them nonetheless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T23:47:51-08:00","id":1353717,"title":"","content":"In my opinion it is a very good move from White Wolf/Paradox. First of all it might bring refreshment to setting. New team with no ties to old WW company and creators, That is blessing for the game. <br /> The meat of the game is(again in my opinion) the story and plot with fresh ideas, Trailer is something new, something exciting. All tribes failed? All right, bring it on. The game might be darker and radical. If garou declare all out war against Weaver tribe (mankind) and other enemies I'm on the hype train. And NO, I don't think that the full scale conflict was already introduced in all the past books. Litany made it shadow war. I guess that many thing will be rewrited according to the trailer including litany,<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T00:05:42-08:00","id":1353723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353717#post1353717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is blessing for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? New perspectives are good, but old perspectives have value too. What if Hunters and Renegade get too caught up in making it &quot;WtA proper&quot; because they don't have the experience Onyx Path's team does with how far you can push things without getting too many people to toss it out as not &quot;really WtA&quot; any more? Onyx Path's track record with the CofD 2e books shows exactly what a mix of new ideas and experience can achieve rather than just a stale repeat of what was before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T00:29:32-08:00","id":1353725,"title":"","content":"Because Onyx Path made excellent W20 and quite good supplements for it (including Book of Wyrm and excluding Changing ways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). They had their run and I'm bit sad that WW cancelled new books and made Shattered dreams unofficial. And it's time for something new. WW's job is to direct WtA 5 creators in way WW wish. There are as many ,,WtA propers&quot; as players. WtA was in stagnation from a lot of time, It's like with V5. Many hate it but I've already seen NEW players that like it a lot. The same might be with WtA. The game shouldn't be made directly for old fanbase cause fanbase yes's and no's dictates what the game should look like in the eyes of ,,experienced&quot; fans. And the new one should shut their mouths and listen to veterans cause they are right because they are ... right! I would rebuild it for new fans without looking back at barking of old dogs. Inlcuding me. Im excited because it might be different than I expected. And that rekindled flame of passion for this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 12-09-2019, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T00:48:28-08:00","id":1353727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353725#post1353725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because Onyx Path made excellent W20 and quite good supplements for it (including Book of Wyrm and excluding Changing ways <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). They had their run and I'm bit sad that WW cancelled new books and made Shattered dreams unofficial. And it's time for something new. WW's job is to direct WtA 5 creators in way WW wish. There are as many ,,WtA propers&quot; as players. WtA was in stagnation from a lot of time, It's like with V5. Many hate it but I've already seen NEW players that like it a lot. The same might be with WtA. The game shouldn't be made directly for old fanbase cause fanbase yes's and no's dictates what the game should look like in the eyes of ,,experienced&quot; fans. And the new one should shut their mouths and listen to veterans cause they are right because they are ... right! I would rebuild it for new fans without looking back at barking of old dogs. Inlcuding me. Im excited because it might be different than I expected. And that rekindled flame of passion for this game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The thing I don't get about this is why not just make a new game about werewolves if your going to change everything about a game.<br /> <br /> We definetely disagree about 'stagnation'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:14:47-08:00","id":1353729,"title":"","content":"The new game was made and it is Werewolf the Forsaken. I'm not going to change anything because I'm not developer or WtA creator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:32:14-08:00","id":1353731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353729#post1353729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new game was made and it is Werewolf the Forsaken. I'm not going to change anything because I'm not developer or WtA creator.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> O.....K.......<br /> <br /> Theres a communication issue here I don't think we're gonna solve any time soon, so I'll leave you to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:32:54-08:00","id":1353732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353725#post1353725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's time for something new.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different people working on it doesn't mean we'll get something &quot;new.&quot; The same people working on it doesn't mean we'll get a repeat of the &quot;old&quot; either.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path only &quot;had their run,&quot; because WW took it away from them. They were gearing up for a new edition of the WoD before Paradox bought the IPs, so we never got to see what their vision for things would have actually been.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are as many ,,WtA propers&quot; as players. </div> </div> </div>That's missing the point.<br /> <br /> A new team that's not as familiar with the material is more likely to be risk adverse towards things fans perceive as sacred cows of the game and changing them. They have something to prove in this situation that a mixed group of freelancers wouldn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> WtA was in stagnation from a lot of time,... </div> </div> </div>Nobody's arguing that WtA doesn't need a new edition.<br /> <br /> I'm questioning the logic of having an entirely brand new team take the reins of a game. WtA wasn't in stagnation because of who was writing it (which has changed multiple times over many years) but because, first the WoD was ended, and then the 20th books weren't meant to be major updates to the games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Many hate it but I've already seen NEW players that like it a lot. </div> </div> </div>Great. Now imagine how much better V5 would be if it had better appeal and new players didn't go looking for people to play with and find there being a massive heated edition divide in the older fans.<br /> <br /> There have been new players coming to the WoD via the 20th books too... that's simply not the only important thing.<br /> <br /> V5 also has something Onyx Path alone can't do, and Hunters can't do either: the reach Paradox can fund. I assure you that even without a massive overhaul, if Paradox decided to get the WoD back in the spotlight with pared down versions of the 20th cores, we'd be seeing an increase in new players from exposure alone.<br /> <br /> The &quot;new people, new version of the game, massive increase in sales,&quot; narrative doesn't work on it's own.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The game shouldn't be made directly for old fanbase cause fanbase yes's and no's dictates what the game should look like in the eyes of ,,experienced&quot; fans. And the new one should shut their mouths and listen to veterans cause they are right because they are ... right! </div> </div> </div>What does this have to do with getting people that have never worked on a WtA game, or a WoD game, before being a &quot;blessing&quot; for the game?<br /> <br /> You're assuming all sorts of things based on this news, but it doesn't really show any actual line of thinking that connects them.<br /> <br /> A new edition of WtA doesn't have to pick between old fans and new fans; it can appeal to both. But that's exactly why you need people that know the game working on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that rekindled flame of passion for this game. </div> </div> </div>Well, my passion for WtA didn't need rekindling after two decades. So what about everyone like me that doesn't want to have our passion for it snuffed out because what we love about it was tossed out for some random new vision for the game? Why should we be ignored exactly?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> I'll try to take this one up too<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353729#post1353729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The new game was made and it is Werewolf the Forsaken. I'm not going to change anything because I'm not developer or WtA creator.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the Forsaken really don't have anything to do with this. The point is that W5 needs to actually be a WtA game or it's going to repeat all the anger V5 stirred up by failing to balance appealing to most of both the old and new fans.<br /> <br /> The problem is that WW decided that the WoD was the brand to back, because it had more name recognition, even if realistically speaking the CofD is actually more the game they'd rather WoD5 be. Paradox is stuck with that choice because otherwise they'd have to take the massive PR hit of ending V5 and starting all over despite having two major video games in the works.<br /> <br /> People that want something different from WtA but similar have that in Forsaken. We don't need something calling itself WtA that's as different from old WtA as Forsaken is from old WtA. We need a new edition of WtA.<br /> <br /> The &quot;you&quot; you're responding to was the general you, not the personal you. Damian didn't mean you, werewolf43, specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 12-09-2019, 04:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T01:58:39-08:00","id":1353737,"title":"","content":"1. I'm aware why Onyx Path ended WtA stuff and that they were planing the new WoD eidtions. I'm aware that WW's trying to make WoD top game again. Thing is that many on this forum including You seems to think that OP and WW have monopoly on WoD and puting game in any other company's hands is abomination. Cause new guys might bring new ideas different from Your view. I am afraid of that too but the licence is in the Paradox hands, they are doing with it what they want. Different people might include new fresh ideas and that would be blessing for stagnation.<br /> <br /> 2. . Familiarity with game material. I think that there are some thing that WW won't allow and spaces that they demand to change. I have faith in new team creativity but under the eye of WW. And I don;t think they will start to work without knowing anything with old material<br /> <br /> 3. The thing with old and new players is silmple. The old players are mature people now. New players I know are kids I used to be, I'd like to be but I'm not anymore. They don't argue like olders about really unimportand things like You and I are doing right now, they sit and play - that's how I see it in my city and among fresh players I've met. <br /> <br /> 4. ,,You're assuming all sorts of things based on this news, but it doesn't really show any actual line of thinking that connects them.&quot; right, I'm always writing chaoticly, but it's the lack of english skills in writing, it's annoying for me that I can't express myself and write all the things I'd like to, but english isn't my first language and I've learned some of it by myself only.<br /> <br /> 5. It could be for old and new and it is not so difficult. Messing with the plot and world and past of storyline will be horrific for old players. System for new ones is tabula rasa, they start from beginning. The question is , should the makers care about old fans ? Only if WW wish it.<br /> <br /> 6. So what about everyone like me that doesn't want to have our passion for rekindled love snuffed out because what we hope about it was tossed out for some sticking to old fanbase vision for the game? Why should we be ignored exactly?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T02:10:54-08:00","id":1353739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353732#post1353732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, the Forsaken really don't have anything to do with this. The point is that W5 needs to actually be a WtA game or it's going to repeat all the anger V5 stirred up by failing to balance appealing to most of both the old and new fans.<br /> <br /> The problem is that WW decided that the WoD was the brand to back, because it had more name recognition, even if realistically speaking the CofD is actually more the game they'd rather WoD5 be. Paradox is stuck with that choice because otherwise they'd have to take the massive PR hit of ending V5 and starting all over despite having two major video games in the works.<br /> <br /> People that want something different from WtA but similar have that in Forsaken. We don't need something calling itself WtA that's as different from old WtA as Forsaken is from old WtA. We need a new edition of WtA.<br /> <br /> The &quot;you&quot; you're responding to was the general you, not the personal you. Damian didn't mean you, werewolf43, specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my misunderstanding, I aspologize.<br /> <br /> I agree! We should get WtA. It was is and should be Werewolf the Apocalypse, not Forsaken. I want the tribes, the lore, the breeds, all 5 patronats. The change I am hoping for is this. The game is quite old for an rpg. I'd like to read about garou struggling in modern world. World that made great leap, big progress in science, technology, pollution of the planet, corruption, and other things I would call dehumanization. I'd like to see garou in nowdays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T02:44:12-08:00","id":1353744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353737#post1353737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is that many on this forum including You seems to think that OP and WW have monopoly on WoD and puting game in any other company's hands is abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>This needling exaggeration does you nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have faith in new team creativity but under the eye of WW. </div> </div> </div>Based on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The old players are mature people now. New players I know are kids I used to be, I'd like to be but I'm not anymore. </div> </div> </div>These simplistic generalizations are also useless. People are people. There are people coming to the WoD TT RPGs despite being older, and younger people well steeped in all this Internet drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...it's annoying for me that I can't express myself and write all the things I'd like to, but english isn't my first language and I've learned some of it by myself only. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate that. But in my experience dealing with things in languages that I learned later in life, keep it simple if you're feel like you're not being understood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be for old and new and it is not so difficult. </div> </div> </div>I never said that. The fact that it is difficult is exactly why I don't like the idea of people that have never worked on WtA doing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Messing with the plot and world and past of storyline will be horrific for old players. </div> </div> </div><br /> No. It's all a matter of execution. I've dealt with multiple editions of metaplot, setting changes, and retcons. The idea that it might happen doesn't horrify me. Who's in charge of it right now has, however, destroyed my confidence that it will go well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353739#post1353739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree! We should get WtA. It was is and should be Werewolf the Apocalypse, not Forsaken. I want the tribes, the lore, the breeds, all 5 patronats. The change I am hoping for is this. The game is quite old for an rpg. I'd like to read about garou struggling in modern world. World that made great leap, big progress in science, technology, pollution of the planet, corruption, and other things I would call dehumanization. I'd like to see garou in nowdays.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which... doesn't really explain why you think a brand new team is so valuable to the game. You're talking about all this potential change, but now talking about just moving the game forward in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T03:18:03-08:00","id":1353749,"title":"","content":"1. Based not on Icarus but on Kids on bikes. They handled the game of strange things pretty well.<br /> 2. Age generalisation isn't as usless as You think. There's rift between generations much more wider then in past ages. The general thinking is different between people in my age and their kids and they are much more separete in opinions then my grandgrandfather children was to him. And it is the same in rpg world.<br /> 3. Messing with plot is terryfing in eyes of peoples I talked to. Retcons , setting changes didn't waved Your confidence and appearance of new designers destroyed Your confidence? Still the game is named WtA by licence owner. You are not being afraid of retocons and similar things but by the peoples who would take the system in their hands and they have no experinece with it? Why? Maby new perspective is necessary. Maby they will se something veterans missed and that would make the game better?<br /> 4. But moving the game foreward in time is a big change isn't it? I'm counting on ideas of men who learn the system past stories and plots. Sticking with the old designers could be a issue with making exactly the same plot adventures and things but 20 years later, Eating their own tails. There have to be compatibility with V5 cause WW won't let them do something other. And after discussions after V5 releasing they can't afford the same mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 12-09-2019, 06:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T04:39:00-08:00","id":1353761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353749#post1353749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Based not on Icarus but on Kids on bikes. They handled the game of strange things pretty well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kids on Bikes is a great game... but it's extremely far from what W5 is going to be. We don't even know if Jon and Doug are working on W5. It's not a new edition of an existing property. It's not a licensed game under an existing company, it's an awesome indie game... which is an entirely different thing than what Paradox is asking for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's rift between generations much more wider then in past ages. </div> </div> </div>Said basically every generation throughout history. I don't see any real reason to put any stock in this.<br /> <br /> There are points in history where there really is a big change in how people think, but it's not as simple as one generation vs. another. Most recently would be the Internet and how it changes how people process information, but it's not about what year you were born it, but when the Internet became part of your cultural experience.<br /> <br /> So, there is a rift around whether or not you had the Internet as a kid (which I did even when a lot of my friends didn't because it's not just age), but it's a hiccup in the course of every generation being different from the previous generation in mostly the same way, not some real trend in generational relations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Retcons , setting changes didn't waved Your confidence and appearance of new designers destroyed Your confidence? </div> </div> </div>No, the execution of changes done under WW/Paradox's watch has destroyed my confidence in their judgement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are not being afraid of retocons and similar things but by the peoples who would take the system in their hands and they have no experinece with it? Why? Maby new perspective is necessary. Maby they will se something veterans missed and that would make the game better? </div> </div> </div>This is a false choice. Paradox doesn't have to pick between just veterans, or just new designers. They can gather a group that combines them. Onyx Path actually does this all the time, but it's not as obvious because the veterans are generally the ones leading the effort. If you look at things like W20 core vs. the W20 supplements you'll see a very big shift in who actually did the books from a bunch of WtA veterans to mostly newer freelancers.<br /> <br /> There is no reason we can't have both... both is actually the best option, because you want to maximize the perspectives at the design meetings, not cut some out arbitrarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But moving the game foreward in time is a big change isn't it? </div> </div> </div>It's as big or as little as you want it to be. The only reason W5 is going to be towards the big by default is because it needs to match V5's approach of &quot;we thought it was the End Times, but it wasn't what we thought that meant,&quot; thing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T05:21:16-08:00","id":1353768,"title":"","content":",,If you look at things like W20 core vs. the W20 supplements you'll see a very big shift in who actually did the books from a bunch of WtA veterans to mostly newer freelancers&quot;.- I agree. You convinced me with this. The W20 core is a very VERY good game and VERY well written. Book of Wyrm for anniversary is a very good suplement and I enjoyed it same shattered dreams. But other stuff isn't as good as them.<br /> <br /> Paradox doesn't have to pick between just veterans, or just new designers. They can gather a group that combines them - We have what we have, If they managed to do cool game they could do this again, but this time in known and popular setting, just why not? But with this let's talk about creators. Who should do the game. If You would make a team of WtA 5ed creators who would be there? I have my own wishlist: Weaver stuff - M. Pondsmith. Wyrm section - fellows from Helmgast (Kult) or Gentelman Gamer. Tribes stuff - B. Bridges. Storyline - ? Wyld - ?<br /> <br /> No, the execution of changes done under WW/Paradox's watch has destroyed my confidence in their judgement. - What exaclty are You writing about? Give few examples, cause it's interesting what You write.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:26:41-08:00","id":1353892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353717#post1353717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my opinion it is a very good move from White Wolf/Paradox. First of all it might bring refreshment to setting. New team with no ties to old WW company and creators, That is blessing for the game.<br /> The meat of the game is(again in my opinion) the story and plot with fresh ideas, Trailer is something new, something exciting. All tribes failed? All right, bring it on. The game might be darker and radical. If garou declare all out war against Weaver tribe (mankind) and other enemies I'm on the hype train. And NO, I don't think that the full scale conflict was already introduced in all the past books. Litany made it shadow war. I guess that many thing will be rewrited according to the trailer including litany,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I bet you liked the Spellplague too, didn't you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:30:22-08:00","id":1353893,"title":"","content":"What is Spellplague? Ok I just checked. I'm not familiar with dnd I.don't.know the world story and events and I don't play dnd. So.I don't know if.I would.like it. But if I would play dnd and like it what would that suppose to mean about me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 12-09-2019, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T10:59:56-08:00","id":1353900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353893#post1353893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is Spellplague? Ok I just checked. I'm not familiar with dnd I.don't.know the world story and events and I don't play dnd. So.I don't know if.I would.like it. But if I would play dnd and like it what would that suppose to mean about me?</div> </div> </div> </div>What they did with the Forgotten Realms back then was quite close to what WW did with V5 and what you'd like to see from W5. Basically, a major rewrite of a long-standing setting, to fit the new team's vision of the game more and to &quot;make it fresh and exciting&quot;.<br /> <br /> Making the assumption that you'd liked it wasn't a judgemental thing on my part. Some people like radical changes and shakeups for long-running settings and stories. Others prefer story advancement and setting changes in smaller doses, while the outlook of the setting doesn't change &quot;that much&quot; on the whole from one edition to the next. It seemed to me that you're in the first group, while I, for example, am in the second. Many fans are. As fans being fans, many of them tend to like the product for what and how it is and reacts negatively for radical changes, <i>exactly</i> because they liked it as it was. That's not the same as wanting no changes at all, mind you.<br /> <br /> Revised Mage's Avatar Storm was another example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 12-09-2019, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:44:31-08:00","id":1353914,"title":"","content":"I'm in my own category group.of.people. I like when things are.moving.foreward. I.like acceptable changes. Changing.ways for.example.was like iron hammer smashed on my balls - unacceptable. All the writings in forum I do is my wishful thinking. My own and only mine. I'm not representing anyone just myself. I am not blind on arguments many people write and during discussion some.of them are convincing.me -. Like Heavy Arms. But I'm living too long to.not have my own opinions and ideas. <br /> Hunters made well acclaimed kids on bikes and.medicore icarus , outbrake i just don't know. Indie games are.much more different then for example WoD setting. But why not to allow them to try. Look at Wrath and glory. Ulisses had fine idea that did not work well. They put their work.at.Cubicle7 hands. We do not.know if Hunter developers would consult their ideas with old creators or.stop making WtA5 cause it would be too difficult for them to.make. Today we know that they will make new edition. Few weeks.ago we didn't know that it would happen then they announced that they will make the game and now they introduced company responsible for that. We.do not know terms.and.conditions of contract. Did You expected that OP would be the chosen.Company? They would make WtA5 announcement earlier then in November. I think that they had the.posibility but question is who did not accepted other side terms. Maby WtA5 old creator said &quot;shit we're too old for this stuff and many things killed the love.for the game in us?&quot; maby hunter was the only.company who agreed to make the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T14:35:27-08:00","id":1353965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353768#post1353768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...just why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as I've said, I think having a mix optimizes thought brought to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Who should do the game. </div> </div> </div>This really doesn't demonstrate an idea of how these game are made. These are games made by lots of people at different levels. There isn't just &quot;this person does X, that person does Y, and another person does Z.&quot; Someone's above them keeping it all one thing. There's coordination with the owners, art/layout, and editing folks.<br /> <br /> Someone might write the best Wyrm creatures, but if they can't work with the lead designer we get a worse book in the end than if you'd taken the second best Wyrm creature writer who can work with the lead.<br /> <br /> W20 Changing Ways was full of good WtA writers, and is a bad book because of disagreements between the book's developer and WW.<br /> <br /> Assembling a team needs to keep in mind that it's a team, not just picking people off a list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What exaclty are You writing about? Give few examples, cause it's interesting what You write. </div> </div> </div>Um... pretty much everything WW/Paradox have done?<br /> <br /> Paradox started by giving WW an extremely wide berth to do what they wanted with the WoD, severely misjudging the team that Martin formed. And despite a lot of us shouting warnings about things, they ignored it until it was too late.<br /> <br /> Now Paradox has reabsorbed WW, but is shopping everything around, leading to a lot of tonal dissonance (even with well received products like Chicago 5th) between books. The stuff released by WW, the stuff released by Modiphius, and the stuff released by Onyx Path all feel noticeably different, which makes me question Paradox's role as overseeing all this to maintain a consistent brand. Now we have a brand new group coming in too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353914#post1353914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm in my own category group.of.people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind you just were extolling the virtue of generalizing about people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But why not to allow them to try. </div> </div> </div>But this is back to a false choice. If someone at Hunters or Renegade was a major choice for this project, nothing stops them for making the W5 core book under WW/Paradox, and then if well received use that goodwill to move the supplements to Hunters like Onyx Path is doing V5 supplements.<br /> <br /> Letting them try has it's limits as an argument, because it's appealing to potential instead of the tangible. It's not like if we don't let them try now, they will never be allowed to try again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did You expected that OP would be the chosen.Company? </div> </div> </div>Nope. Pretty much every response I saw to Paradox not announcing the company when they announced W5 was that they'd have said if it was Modiphius or Onyx Path... so who's going to actually be doing this.<br /> <br /> I was honestly expecting Ulisses until Hunters was announced. They seemed a solid choice and Bill Bridges working with them would have avoided... well... all this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> maby hunter was the only.company who agreed to make the game? </div> </div> </div>I seriously doubt Onyx Path would have actually said no considering they make V5 books already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:48:31-08:00","id":1353981,"title":"","content":"So.. Paradox has a division that is White Wolf. White wolf liscences the WOD, Cod, Exalted etc. White Wolf/Paradox tapped Hunters to make W5. Hunters in turn tapped a smaller Studio as they like Whitewolf proper are just basically a liscencer for smaller studios? So Hunter in turn has tapped Renegade studios that seems to have little to no experience with making PnP games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:14:21-08:00","id":1353990,"title":"","content":"From the interview I saw, it looks like Hunters is making the game and Renegade is just distributing. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eIKNlLvQYqc\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eIKNlLvQYqc</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 12-09-2019, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:09:55-08:00","id":1354017,"title":"","content":"What has Hunters done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:30:38-08:00","id":1354023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353981#post1353981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.. Paradox has a division that is White Wolf. White wolf liscences the WOD, Cod, Exalted etc. White Wolf/Paradox tapped Hunters to make W5. Hunters in turn tapped a smaller Studio as they like Whitewolf proper are just basically a liscencer for smaller studios? So Hunter in turn has tapped Renegade studios that seems to have little to no experience with making PnP games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Renegade is actually a larger studio when you look at their pool of creatives; but Renegade has more focus on board and card games than RPGs. Hunters and Renegade also do all of their PnP games together, so there's no real shock there. Both are relatively new companies, so their lack of back catalog isn't as bad when you look at some of the people that work for them have been at this for a long time.<br /> <br /> The lack of experience is more around professional work in the WoD environment, or working on licensed properties, over developing their own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:33:05-08:00","id":1354025,"title":"","content":"Outbreak: Undead, Kids on Bikes, and Icarus are Hunters three PnP RPGs. The also have some non-gaming books that are gaming adjacent under their belts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T18:46:15-08:00","id":1354030,"title":"","content":"This thread has done nothing but made me cringe and turn away from w5 like a man paranoid about someone socking him in the junk. All they had to do, was work off of the 20th Anniversary editions, make metaplot advancements/changes that made sense and were with the spirit of the game. Thats it. V5 fucked that up hard, W5 will fuck that up HARDER. Like the worst of the metaplot and fluff we got in 1st ed bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T21:16:29-08:00","id":1354059,"title":"","content":"If V5 is any kind of indicator, then I have no reason to believe that I will like or recognize whatever W5 turns out to be. I'm sure it will be a fine game about werewolves with various <i>nominal</i> similarities to <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>'s (as it existed in its various editions through 20th anniversary), but I find it hard to believe that it be W:tA in spirit--i.e., in tone, aesthetic, theme, what have you.<br /> <br /> I would start a joking-but-not-joking &quot;wrong answers only&quot;-type thread dedicated solely to coming up with all the cringe-y and disappointing things that will happen with W5 (based on the assumption that the change will be comparable to that which occurred with V5,) but, frankly, that would simply be a depressing spiral of negativity. Every time I try to think of an absurd or bizarre hypothetical change to kick off the thread, I just make myself sad because I end up thinking, &quot;aww, hell, they might actually <i>do</i> that.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm waiting for the day that someone (or maybe many someones) will dedicate some time, thought, and care to writing Storyteller Vault supplements intended to modernize whatever aspects of the various classic gamelines need to be updated in order to conform to modern technology, and global politics. Not even metaplot developments (because I feel like a fan supplement purporting to expand upon the metaplot would not necessarily have wide appeal,) just well-reasoned extrapolations of what certain aspects of the game(s) might look like if the game(s) had been written in 20XX. In technology alone, shit has gotten <i>so </i>wild and different in just the time since M20 was published--let alone V20! Let's face it, no one in 2015 would have thought that FB would be <i>instrumental </i>in a <b>literal genocide</b>, or that FB and Twitter would one day be considered some of the primary contributing factors/tools in the election of the most divisive POTUS in over a century, or the resurgence of open and notorious white supremacy in public spaces. Mind you, I'm sure we're all doing this individually at our own tables as time wears on, if only as a matter of necessity (except those of us playing period games which will never require &quot;modernizing&quot;,) but I'm willing to bet someone is doing it much better than I am.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 12-10-2019, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T21:25:43-08:00","id":1354061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354059#post1354059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If V5 is any kind of indicator, then I have no reason to believe that I will like or recognize whatever W5 turns out to be. I'm sure it will be a fine game about werewolves with various <i>nominal</i> similarities to <i>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</i>'s (as it existed in its various editions through 20th anniversary), but I find it hard to believe that it be W:tA in spirit--i.e., in tone, aesthetic, theme, what have you.<br /> <br /> I would start a joking-but-not-joking &amp;quot;wrong answers only&amp;quot;-type thread dedicated solely to coming up with all the cringe-y and disappointing things that will happen with W5 (based on the assumption that the change will be comparable to that which occurred with V5,) but, frankly, that would simply be a depressing spiral of negativity. Every time I try to think of an absurd or bizarre hypothetical change to kick off the thread, I just make myself sad because I end up thinking, &amp;quot;aww, hell, they might actually <i>do</i> that.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I'm waiting for the day that someone (or maybe many someones) will dedicate some time, thought, and care to writing Storyteller Vault supplements intended to modernize whatever aspects of the various classic gamelines need to be updated in order to conform to modern technology, and global politics. Not even metaplot developments (because I feel like a fan supplement purporting to expand upon the metaplot would not necessarily have wide appeal,) just well-reasoned extrapolations of what certain aspects of the game(s) might look like if the game(s) had been written in 20XX. In technology alone, shit has gotten <i>so </i>wild and different in just the time since M20 was published--let alone V20! Let's face it, no one in 2015 would have thought that FB would be <i>instrumental </i>in a <b>literal genocide</b>, or that FB and Twitter would one day be considered some of the primary contributing factors/tools in the election of the most divisive POTUS in over a century, or the resurgence of open and notorious white supremacy in public spaces. Mind you, I'm sure we're all doing this individually at our own tables as time wears on, if only as a matter of necessity (except those of us playing period games which will never require &amp;quot;modernizing&amp;quot;,) but I'm willing to bet someone is doing it much better than I am.</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah pretty much that. Hell theres a guy that is making armory books for the x20 games. Bought one with Old West weapons since im running a Wyld West gane soon","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T22:15:00-08:00","id":1354065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354061#post1354061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...yeah pretty much that. Hell theres a guy that is making armory books for the x20 games. Bought one with Old West weapons since im running a Wyld West gane soon</div> </div> </div> </div> Storyteller's Vault is the best thing to happen to Classic World of Darkness since the 20th anniversary lines took off. I am <i>REALLY</i> looking forward to seeing what people come up with as times goes by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T22:53:29-08:00","id":1354070,"title":"","content":"Gonna put my predictions down now for what we can expect 10005% to see in W5, setting-wise:<br /> <br /> ~The BSDs all ran away to fight a something in the most inhospitable corner of the world; Idaho. With them went everyone over Rank 2.<br /> ~Ronin become more prominent and instead of gifts they have Ronin Inscription, allowing them to make scrolls that have gifts on them that they can use.<br /> ~Pentex also goes to fight the something in forgotten, uninhabited, inhospitable Idaho, but then they didn't. They merged with every other all the businesses to become the megacorp &quot;Third Impergium&quot; for no reason at all and no connection with any past or future Impergiums. None of the marketting department who came up with the branding of the megacorp know what an Impergium is, but they thought it sounded cool.<br /> ~The Amazon basin, all of Africa and the warzone hellscape of Idaho have seen the total elimination of all shifters due to the actions of the Third Impergium. Your caern's next, yo!<br /> <br /> IDK, that's all the salt I have right now. I'll see you all after breakfast tomorrow. Stay out of Idaho, k?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":700,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","user":"Vysha","date":". 12-10-2019, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T00:16:04-08:00","id":1354080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354070#post1354070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna put my predictions down now for what we can expect 10005% to see in W5, setting-wise:<br /> <br /> ~The BSDs all ran away to fight a something in the most inhospitable corner of the world; Idaho. With them went everyone over Rank 2.<br /> ~Ronin become more prominent and instead of gifts they have Ronin Inscription, allowing them to make scrolls that have gifts on them that they can use.<br /> ~Pentex also goes to fight the something in forgotten, uninhabited, inhospitable Idaho, but then they didn't. They merged with every other all the businesses to become the megacorp &amp;quot;Third Impergium&amp;quot; for no reason at all and no connection with any past or future Impergiums. None of the marketting department who came up with the branding of the megacorp know what an Impergium is, but they thought it sounded cool.<br /> ~The Amazon basin, all of Africa and the warzone hellscape of Idaho have seen the total elimination of all shifters due to the actions of the Third Impergium. Your caern's next, yo!<br /> <br /> IDK, that's all the salt I have right now. I'll see you all after breakfast tomorrow. Stay out of Idaho, k?</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who has a friend from Idaho, what is your beef with Potato Land?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T06:36:38-08:00","id":1354131,"title":"","content":"I'm excited to see what will be the aftermath of the Garou attack on Malfeas. How will Glasswalkers and Weaver spirits handle this new time of internet surveillance? Will the Red Talons, the closest of the tribes to wild nature, stay sane or lose themselves to despair or madness? With the rise of the Gehenna War among the Kindred in Mesopotamia and the current geo-political chaos of the Middle East, will the Children of Gaia try to evacuate their Kin from their traditional homeland, or dive into efforts to try and heal it? Will the Stargazers return to the Garou Nation? Have the supernatural chaos of the &quot;End of Days&quot; impacted the Silent Striders' curse? Will the Silver Fangs tendency toward madness change, weaken or grow worse as Gaia weakens?<br /> Also, will Pentex team up with the Second Inquisition and Technocracy???","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T07:48:24-08:00","id":1354144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354080#post1354080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who has a friend from Idaho, what is your beef with Potato Land?</div> </div> </div> </div>Idaho knows what it did. Idaho knows how it can fix things between me and that state. It's Idaho's move. I can't get into it any more than that, it's too painful of a memory to revisit here. Too soon, my mouse. Too soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T09:01:08-08:00","id":1354170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354070#post1354070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna put my predictions down now for what we can expect 10005% to see in W5, setting-wise:<br /> <br /> ~The BSDs all ran away to fight a something in the most inhospitable corner of the world; Idaho. With them went everyone over Rank 2.</div> </div> </div> </div> Damn you, this will probably only be the beginning. Even odds that the few Garou left are all so noobish that no one remembers how to do half of the rituals, what kind of behavior is credited with which sorts of renown, and even if they fall ass backwards into renown by accidentally burning down an O'Tolley's while they're stoned, they still won't be able to find anyone to challenge for their next rank, or (if they do rank somehow) have any institutional knowledge of what gifts they can get at the new rank, or which spirits teach it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T08:41:48-08:00","id":1354370,"title":"","content":"The trailer is quite clear about the message.<br /> The tribes have failed. <br /> I want to see total, radical, war. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:11:39-08:00","id":1354398,"title":"","content":"And I'm pretty sure a lot of us would like WtA not to be reduced to just one thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T10:16:14-08:00","id":1354400,"title":"","content":"Total radical war doesn't mean that other things would be thrown away. Desperation and shame leaks from trailer. Failure is obvious, failing lead.to shame in front of Gaia, Tribe, Pack and the.mirror. and it.leads to rage and fury.<br /> The spiritual part is so far big question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:16:09-08:00","id":1354458,"title":"","content":"You know, there was another WoD game that decided that there was a failure state to an essential question of the game line before, and that a lot of things were being shaken up.<br /> <br /> It was Mage Revised. Only, Werewolf doesn't usually lose focus or feet on the ground like the Horizon-centered M:tA did, so it seems like a thoroughly unnecessary step to update the game. Much like how the Avatar Storm was suddenly retconned applied to Garou and Fera in Changing Ways. So, total war looks like it's off, in favor of whatever conflicts were like in MRev. If some antagonist faction, say as an example, goes so far as to start putting Garou brains into cyborg bodies (in spite of how, you know, becoming a Drone was pretty much already like that in spiritual terms) and using them as shock troops, I will not be surprised in the least. I will be doubly disappointed, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:31:45-08:00","id":1354463,"title":"","content":"Literally we could have just had Pentex get Trust Busted and have a gazillioin other contenders to the throne. Making it even harder to take em down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T14:43:02-08:00","id":1354467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354398#post1354398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm pretty sure a lot of us would like WtA not to be reduced to just one thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>and exactly who the hell said such a thing?<br /> I said what I want to see, and what I want to see includes a LOT of things.<br /> If total war on a world that is dying is a simple thing that doesn't include critical views regarding enviroment, moral crisis among the tribes, emotional struggle and even a more intense sense of despair and tragedy, and another tons of things, I'm Santa Claus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 12-11-2019, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:42:33-08:00","id":1354486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354463#post1354463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally we could have just had Pentex get Trust Busted and have a gazillioin other contenders to the throne. Making it even harder to take em down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, it was always harder to take down every Wyrm-Influenced Corporation, but for the same reason that Pentex won't get trust-busted - the corporations have too much of a death grip on what laws get passed and when they apply in various countries, particularly the US. Pentex would fall, but having it sink would leave all of the others in a bad way due to running interference, so the other WICs are probably playing things safe and not actively trying to throw away their shield.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T16:53:18-08:00","id":1354493,"title":"","content":"&quot;Total, radical war,&quot; is an all consuming setting element, or it's not total. Total war is when there cease to be boundaries between war and not-war, where there are no civilians because all of society is part of the war effort, where there are no rules of engagement or agreements to restrict weapons of mass destruction, and so on; there is only victory or death and everything else is furthering those efforts or ignored.<br /> <br /> If the setting gets to total war, there ceases to be anything but total war. That's why it's called total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T19:00:19-08:00","id":1354509,"title":"","content":"My only concern about TOTAL FARGING WAR is that - if the result is anything like V5 - only half of the tribes will be offered as playable. If the Garou Nation splits down the middle over the question of whether to reinaugurate the Impergium, as was hinted when V5 was first announced, then the books that end up seeing print will only cover character creation and lore for the half of the nation that does not want to kill all the hyoo-mons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T14:06:43-08:00","id":1354666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354463#post1354463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally we could have just had Pentex get Trust Busted and have a gazillioin other contenders to the throne. Making it even harder to take em down.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Disney, Nestle and Berkshire Hathaway don't get trust busted IRL, then I can't see how Pentex would. In oWoD, of all places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25584-logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","name":"Logoth\u00e9t\u0113s","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25584_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T00:07:22-08:00","id":1354730,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/werewolf-the-apocalypse\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.huntersentertainment.com...the-apocalypse</a> &quot;<b><i>Werewolf </i></b>is about how we help/hinder each other to survive against great odds,&quot; said Ivan Van Norman, partner and producer of Hunters Entertainment. &quot;This game was the first campaign I ever GM\u2019ed, and I believe its stories are more relevant and impactful now than they\u2019ve ever been - which is why we're excited to bring it back to fans old and new.&quot; - So there is someone who has played the game and know the story behind it.<br /> <br /> Players will play as Garou, individuals born of two worlds, the material and the Umbra (spirit world), who can shapeshift into wolves at will. In <i><b>Werewolf: The Apocalypse</b></i> the world, Gaia, is dying. After many generations, the Garou - Gaia\u2019s chosen warriors and defenders - are divided on how to save the planet, their spiritual mother. Attacked by outside forces and plagued by infighting, each Garou tribe shares different ideologies and goals, which have - up to this point - all failed them in their ultimate goal, to rescue a dying Gaia. - the core of system won't be changed.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the game is set to share a lot of similarities with the recent release of <i><b>Vampire: The Masquerade 5th Edition</b></i> but will have a lot of elements that make it unique. - the game system would be compatibile with V5, I like ,,lot uinique elements&quot; cause I've been worried about gnosis","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T17:51:44-08:00","id":1354839,"title":"","content":"If nothing else, the &quot;lots of unique elements&quot; line ensures that the &quot;which game system is right&quot; threads will continue for at least another edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T03:53:36-08:00","id":1354873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Helur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354370#post1354370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trailer is quite clear about the message.<br /> The tribes have failed.<br /> I want to see total, radical, war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Failure doesn't meen total war.<br /> <br /> Yesterday I've walked a lot and tried to figure out how could all the tribe failed.<br /> <br /> Generaly: Gaia isn't saved, the ecosystem is crumbling, spiececs die out day to day. Caerns loose they potency, maybe even the Fera starts to loose their spiritual Potency.<br /> Less and less Garou are born, Metis is the main Breed. They are breed as needed shock-troops.<br /> The Veil was shattered. The Second Inquisition started to hunt Garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies:</b> Less and less wild placecs remain. Women are still used, abused, threw, and Wyrm uses bigotry on BOTH sides to foster hatred. They number dwindled, and had to accept men into their rank. They identity is shattered<br /> <b>Bone Gnawers:</b> Died out. Lone survivors remain, but the tribe is no more.<br /> <b>Children of Gaia:</b> There is no peace. The Nation is fragmented. But there were successfull. They brought back the Bunyip, or something wearing their skin. They live, breed and figh. The Third War of Rage is brewing in Australia, but now the Garou are on the loosing side.<br /> <b>Fianna:</b> No more boose? Donno. Because of the almost forgotten ties to the Good Folk, Tallain become very intrested in them. Now they are hunted by nightmares and loose ancecstral land to them and the Spirals.<br /> <b>Get of Fenris:</b> There is no epic war to figh. What's their purose now?<br /> <b>Glas Walkers:</b> Technology become a weakness. Men adapted faster, now the system is used against them. The Weaver becomes stronger, the webs thicker. Some of them even started to fall.<br /> <b>Red Talons:</b> Wolves die out. A new Impergium was started and it failed. Human technology was stronger. Drones are unaffected by the Delirium, Hellfire Missiles burns Caerns and meet. The Second Inquisition started to hunt the changers, not just vampires.<br /> <b>Silver Fangs:</b> Heroes die. Fangs lost their power, their blood is diluted. They lost the Crown and influence. No one trusts a fallen leader.<br /> <b>Shadow Lords:</b> Couldn't grab the power. Tried, fought, tore down the Fangs, but what they could achieve is a fragmented Nation. Tribes and Camps without guadiance and leadership.<br /> Silent Striders: Could not break the Curse. Wepauvet was able to connect some Ancestors with newborns, but later other spirits, things used the connections. Nowdays the youth of the tribe is the playground of wraiths.<br /> Stargazers: Tribal homeland was lost, and the Beast Court doesn't accepted them as it was expected. Now they are outcasts.<br /> <b>Uktena:</b> Banes gets free, Storm Eater is aproaching.<br /> <b>Wendigo:</b> The natives are constantly used, abused. More and more Kin is lost to mixed pairing and Wendigo looses it's spiritual &quot;purity&quot;. It's getting more tainted and cannibalism is occuring in alarming frequency.<br /> <br /> Bonus:<br /> <br /> <b>BSDs:</b> Wyrm is not free, Weaver is stronger every day. The Metis population is so high that tht Tribe may die out / weaken in one generation. They are in the focus of Second Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T05:25:01-08:00","id":1354879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354873#post1354873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failure doesn't meen total war.<br /> <br /> Yesterday I've walked a lot and tried to figure out how could all the tribe failed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even for V5, a lot of this is a big stretch. Like the Bone Gnawers have always been the tribe most likely to survive. But then again V5 made so many stretches and disregarded so much I wouldn't be surprised. <br /> <br /> -The Silver fangs maintain their lead by putting queens in charge instead of kings, as opposed to, y'know, the shadow lords taking charge. <br /> The CoG are completely right, the GoF are working with the wyrm, The BF accept non-metis male-to-female transitions, The Fianna have learnt the error of their ways, every tribe has modernized, all the Fera are getting along just fine, Humans somehow don't suffer the delierium any more and are actively hunting the Garou with co-ordination between Wyrm,Weaver and unaligned groups. All the elders have left for the deep umbra, Ronin are just as good as regular garou now, kinfolk too... <br /> <br /> I just don't like the idea of W5 seeing how V5 was. We aught to treat the 5th edition lineup like 4th edition DnD: It was a bad dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T09:45:03-08:00","id":1354895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354879#post1354879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We aught to treat the 5th edition lineup like 4th edition DnD: It was a bad dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad comparison; 4e is the least bad edition of D&amp;D.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T10:34:39-08:00","id":1354902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354879#post1354879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even for V5, a lot of this is a big stretch. Like the Bone Gnawers have always been the tribe most likely to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trailer said every tribe failed. The Gnawers' main objective is to survive. 1+1=Extinction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354879#post1354879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just don't like the idea of W5 seeing how V5 was. We aught to treat the 5th edition lineup like 4th edition DnD: It was a bad dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>I fear this will hijack the topic fast...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T11:38:13-08:00","id":1354907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354902#post1354902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trailer said every tribe failed. The Gnawers' main objective is to survive. 1+1=Extinction.<br /> <br /> <br /> I fear this will hijack the topic fast...</div> </div> </div> </div>Either way, this new edition will suck. Rather than focusing on the best parts they will focus on the worst, cook up new stuff that should have stayed in their test games, the art will be as dogshit as V5's and it wont even be a good coffee table book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T12:27:46-08:00","id":1354911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354902#post1354902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The trailer said every tribe failed. The Gnawers' main objective is to survive. 1+1=Extinction.<br /> ..</div> </div> </div> </div>You've gotta admit this is the most clownish overreaction there is and 'Subverting expectations&quot; is not the wisest of plans for a longrunning RPG. What V5 did to the sects can't be considered popular and the changes they made to, say, the Tremere or Brujah largely doesn't agree with those players who embraced those clans and took them seriously. The BG will be the last tribe to fall and the BF will never accept Trans homids or lupus. I mean the BG have all the survival gifts they can get and the largest number of members. The real world is actually having an increase in wolf numbers so the RT can only really 'fail' if the other tribes compete for their kinfolk to successfully or their human side dies out. The CoG will never unite the garou nation under one tribe or bring peace because that's always been a critical failing of Garou in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T12:39:01-08:00","id":1354912,"title":"","content":"The art is the thing I am worried about. My expectations for WtA is cut to two artists Prescott and Spencer. That is the BASE for fine acceptable art in the core book. Wishlist is another thing so I would like to see Briclot and Bermejo doing the drawings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T12:45:07-08:00","id":1354913,"title":"","content":"There's still nothing to overreact. I've just had too many time to think about nothing. I've tried to find agenda/main object of the tribes. With the BGs it was easy. I don't say that this outcome (I mean ther death) is realistic. Except if the Rats come out to play. <br /> <br /> I'm looking forward this Edition, and hope the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T13:20:23-08:00","id":1354917,"title":"","content":"I agree. Besides my first atempt to imagine tribes failing is something like this but I have already dozens of variations in my mind , few first tribes for example:<br /> <br /> Furies - the fall of main caerns, sacred places acording to lithany. I don't think that the main problem with Furies is.male female.tranagender etc. issues cause I imagine that every sept look different for it. Being mother is a different thing and abortion in young generation would bring huge strife in tribe. Besides it would make struggle between chalices and generations more deadly. The Furies are protectors of life and Wyld so divided as.never before they would fall. And sacred places? In my opinion overrun by great.migration.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers - fall by socialism. In Europe goverments help poorer and homeless by donating mount of.money. They have places to live ,food, clothes. European Gnawers could become lazy and.corrupted by system. They could lost their.purpose when homeles.peoples they were helping suddenly.wouldn't need them anymore. Don't have idea yet about other places.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia - the society ruled by cult of body and money where everything is allowed is very tempting.for hedonist tribe. Drugs, sex, party and the dark shit like child abuse, forced prostitution mixed already and is visible starting from higher society to the bottom of list. CoG had been crossing the line with their rites and.philosophy many times and now where secrets couldn't be secrets anymore the other tribes for example in frustration would tear them apart piece by piece. Think about sin eating rite and.crusading Get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-14T14:20:35-08:00","id":1354925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354917#post1354917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers - fall by socialism. In Europe goverments help poorer and homeless by donating mount of.money. They have places to live ,food, clothes. European Gnawers could become lazy and.corrupted by system. They could lost their.purpose when homeles.peoples they were helping suddenly.wouldn't need them anymore. Don't have idea yet about other places.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, i see the BGs getting hit harder by the opiod and homlessness crisis thats hitting the states hard. Like have you seen California? I live here and its bad. Tweakers and nutjibs everywhere. Now add the Wyrm taint and see how bad it really gets","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T00:41:38-08:00","id":1354969,"title":"","content":"No I didn't. I belive You are right I'm thinking about central ale western europe where I live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T02:51:29-08:00","id":1354973,"title":"","content":"I think you also have the relationship of the Gnawers and the homeless backwards. The Gnawers cause and purpose isn't protecting the homeless. It's making a home where other Garou don't, surviving where it's hard to survive, to fight the Wyrm wherever it dwells. They tend to live with the lowest class humans, because they're the most vulnerable to the Wyrm's corruption of systems and institutions. Social services don't hurt the Gnawers, it just lets them focus their energy on joining with the Glass Walkers and Children of Gaia to start going after larger scale issues (though in Europe the Gnawers would have their hands full with refugee communities that don't have the same access to social services).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T05:09:38-08:00","id":1354982,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure if the Gnawers lost their homeless base (Unlikely, given what's going on in the world) They'd just infiltrate the next poorest communities or move to a place where they're needed. I'm pretty sure countries like Sweden, where outside of a few pro-beggars homelessless virtually doesn't exist and the goverment does more for the environment than other nations, could do with some reshuffling. (House prices in sweden are definitely of the Wyrm, but people have places to stay), Whilst say, the UK could definitely accommodate more Gnawers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T08:51:23-08:00","id":1355013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354912#post1354912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art is the thing I am worried about. My expectations for WtA is cut to two artists Prescott and Spencer. That is the BASE for fine acceptable art in the core book. Wishlist is another thing so I would like to see Briclot and Bermejo doing the drawings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is my biggest concern as the art direction for V5 has been horrendous. Onyx Path's art has been pretty bad too, as of the past few years, now that I think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T14:15:39-08:00","id":1355053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355013#post1355013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is my biggest concern as the art direction for V5 has been horrendous. Onyx Path's art has been pretty bad too, as of the past few years, now that I think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The only Main book that I felt had objectionable art, 20th wise, was DAV20. I don't think mage was great either but it had some good stuff in there and nothing stood out as overwhelmingly bad. Some of the more unimportant works that freelancers chugged out, like Lore of the Bloodlines, had some objectionable stuff, but they had bad writing too so... More relevant supplements like Lore of the Clans or Book of the Wyrm had fantastic art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T19:38:33-08:00","id":1355109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354493#post1354493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Total, radical war,&quot; is an all consuming setting element, or it's not total. Total war is when there cease to be boundaries between war and not-war, where there are no civilians because all of society is part of the war effort, where there are no rules of engagement or agreements to restrict weapons of mass destruction, and so on; there is only victory or death and everything else is furthering those efforts or ignored.<br /> <br /> If the setting gets to total war, there ceases to be anything but total war. That's why it's called total.</div> </div> </div> </div> At the very least, having an edition of Werewolf with a Warhammer ethos (war all day, every day; pew pew rip slash cut war war war), would not be wholly antithetical to what the Garou have basically been gearing up for for literal ages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354895#post1354895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bad comparison; 4e is the least bad edition of D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div> HOT TAKE! I disagree vehemently, but I'm bizarrely pleased that you would just state this so matter-of-fact-ly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-15T21:07:37-08:00","id":1355117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355109#post1355109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the very least, having an edition of Werewolf with a Warhammer ethos (war all day, every day; pew pew rip slash cut war war war), would not be wholly antithetical to what the Garou have basically been gearing up for for literal ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, though the point was the contraction of possible playstyles.<br /> <br /> There's a reason why the setting devolving to this was considered the end of the original run.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I disagree vehemently, but I'm bizarrely pleased that you would just state this so matter-of-fact-ly. </div> </div> </div><br /> This really isn't the thread for a D&amp;D edition war.<br /> <br /> However, we've nicely illustrated why D&amp;D 4e and V5 get a lot of comparisons right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T10:43:53-08:00","id":1355210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355109#post1355109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the very least, having an edition of Werewolf with a Warhammer ethos (war all day, every day; pew pew rip slash cut war war war), would not be wholly antithetical to what the Garou have basically been gearing up for for literal ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd shock the players into apathy and hopelessness rather than/along with their characters, which is probably not something that you want to have happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> HOT TAKE! I disagree vehemently, but I'm bizarrely pleased that you would just state this so matter-of-fact-ly. </div> </div> </div>It helps to have a healthy level of contempt for all editions of D&amp;D, since it forgot what a dire wolf actually was after 1e ended and has a general focus and presentation that feels like sand grains between my foot and a shoe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T11:46:02-08:00","id":1355223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355210#post1355210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps to have a healthy level of contempt for all editions of D&amp;D, since it forgot what a dire wolf actually was after 1e ended and has a general focus and presentation that feels like sand grains between my foot and a shoe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355117#post1355117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This really isn't the thread for a D&amp;D edition war.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just bashing D&amp;D in general. If you have something to say with the D&amp;D comparison that's actually relevant to the thread, by all means, but otherwise... maybe find a different approach to the actual topic at hand?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:54:39-08:00","id":1355240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355223#post1355223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ahem:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Or just bashing D&amp;D in general. If you have something to say with the D&amp;D comparison that's actually relevant to the thread, by all means, but otherwise... maybe find a different approach to the actual topic at hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>There was a very Werewolf-relevant point in that post, since dire wolves were the size of moderately large dogs but thanks to AD&amp;D 2e mixing up dire wolf and worg stat blocks in a Monstrous Compendium entry*, everyone thinks that dire wolves were the size of Hispo, down to Hispo being erroneously labeled &quot;dire wolf form&quot; on too many occasions to count, including in W20. Hopefully, whatever else W5 does, it won't repeat it.<br /> <br /> *In 1e: Dire wolves listed as Size M, with Worgs as Size L; in 2e, dire wolves listed as Size L, with Worgs as Size M. Later editions made them both Size L.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T14:26:12-08:00","id":1355270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355240#post1355240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a very Werewolf-relevant point in that post,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously?<br /> <br /> Dude, just stop. Most of us know about the whole &quot;dire wolf&quot; thing. It's bullshit to try to claim that had <b>anything</b> to do with D&amp;D 4e, or is a defense of something like, &quot;It helps to have a healthy level of contempt for all editions of D&amp;D...&quot;<br /> <br /> If what you actually care about is hoping that W5 doesn't repeat the RPG convention, however bone headed it is, of made up fantasy giant-wolves being labeled as dire wolves despite the real world extinct species known as dire wolves looking nothing like that? Say that so we can move on and not derail things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:31:41-08:00","id":1355311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355270#post1355270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seriously?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why else mention that one point about dire wolves in the face of a sea of anything else that one could pick from?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dude, just stop. Most of us know about the whole &quot;dire wolf&quot; thing. It's bullshit to try to claim that had <b>anything</b> to do with D&amp;D 4e, or is a defense of something like, &quot;It helps to have a healthy level of contempt for all editions of D&amp;D...&quot; </div> </div> </div>Yeah, 4e was more egregious in this regard compared to other editions, but it was the general block of all editions that I was talking about there. At any rate, &quot;most of us&quot; and dire wolf knowledge never seems to be quite as comprehensive as the ideal, given that it did, after all, make it into W20 in place of &quot;the near-wolf&quot;. Also ran into it one the twitter for WW a bit of a ways back, though at least the person I corrected didn't seem too upset about my pedantry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If what you actually care about is hoping that W5 doesn't repeat the RPG convention, however bone headed it is, of made up fantasy giant-wolves being labeled as dire wolves despite the real world extinct species known as dire wolves looking nothing like that? Say that so we can move on and not derail things. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how it wasn't clear, again, given the choice of a single specific thing to mention about a general dislike of D&amp;D before a blanket &quot;this just isn't for me&quot; to cover everything else that wasn't topical.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T19:50:59-08:00","id":1355325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355210#post1355210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It helps to have a healthy level of contempt for all editions of D&amp;D, since it forgot what a dire wolf actually was after 1e ended and has a general focus and presentation that feels like sand grains between my foot and a shoe.</div> </div> </div> </div> I feel like the fact that you don't appear to like D&amp;D writ large makes me want to understand your rationale for thinking 4e is the best even <i>more</i>. Your disdain means that your opinion is not biased by any fondness or nostalgia for the game. Obviously I don't want to clog this thread with D&amp;D talk, but if you have link to another thread where you've already explained your rationale (and I assume there must be one <i>somewhere</i>) I would <u><b>love</b></u> to read it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T22:34:47-08:00","id":1355340,"title":"","content":"So we are in agreement that W5 will probably blow roght? What do you think they will do right though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T08:02:15-08:00","id":1355400,"title":"","content":"Re: Edition war<br /> I understand 4e was mechnically sound, but thematically it just wasn't what people were after. Trying to bring things &quot;back to the roots&quot; (In DnD's case, a wargame) wasn't what people were expecting or what they wanted: The Game had evolved, and as I understand it the Narrative was so reviled it was retconned away next edition.... Yeah, I think the analogy is apt. Only, y'know, DnD 4e actually had some merits to it's design... <br /> <br /> @Brother mouse. <br /> <br /> I Think the hunger system, which does not fit vampire at all, might work very well with rage. The rest is a garbage slide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T10:31:42-08:00","id":1355437,"title":"","content":"Rage doesn't feel like it would actually be a good fit with Hunger as-is. You don't rouse Rage; you witness or experience something, and it riles you up. You'd have to make allowances for individuals and circumstances giving you Rage dice instead of opting to increase your Rage. Because even the player opting to increase the character's Rage doesn't really sound like it shakes out the way that it's supposed to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355340#post1355340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we are in agreement that W5 will probably blow roght? What do you think they will do right though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe they'll finally get around to correcting &quot;Chung Kuel&quot; as a Nuwisha totem, writing in Chung-k'uei if they keep it in Wade-Giles Romanization for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T11:27:40-08:00","id":1355448,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of Hunger not being a bad basis for Rage is that Rage is supposed to be a constant presence in a werewolf's life. There's no escaping it, it can crop up any time, etc. Where a lot of us feel Hunger is too intrusive for vampires, Rage is supposed to be that intrusive. I'd also point out that &quot;Rousing Rage&quot; in this context is when you would spend Rage or roll Rage in the extant rules. The difference in approach would be that instead of spending Rage calming you down, Rousing Rage would drive you to be harder to control.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T16:55:14-08:00","id":1355512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355448#post1355448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the idea of Hunger not being a bad basis for Rage is that Rage is supposed to be a constant presence in a werewolf's life. There's no escaping it, it can crop up any time, etc. Where a lot of us feel Hunger is too intrusive for vampires, Rage is supposed to be that intrusive. I'd also point out that &quot;Rousing Rage&quot; in this context is when you would spend Rage or roll Rage in the extant rules. The difference in approach would be that instead of spending Rage calming you down, Rousing Rage would drive you to be harder to control.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like frenzy territory, not typical Rage use. Rage is supposed to fluctuate and get used, potentially leaving a character vulnerable from depletion or even Losing the Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T17:40:37-08:00","id":1355530,"title":"","content":"WtA as it stands is uneven. If you use Rage in a staredown for a better dice-pool, you risk Frenzy. When you recover from Incapacitated with Rage, you Frenzy, etc. This would ideally also cover things like the Curse and the Beast Within as one mechanic instead of multiple things to remember.<br /> <br /> Losing the Wolf would still be possible, but it would be come from over doing however you'd reduce your Rage, not by whipping your Rage up. Though Losing the Wolf is something I've never seen happen in any WtA game I've played in.. it's almost happened a few times until an experienced player pointed out to a new player to not spend that last point of Rage/Willpower. It's just too easy to avoid, and there's no good reason to risk it.<br /> <br /> Yes, it would be different, but it's functional without radically altering the nature of the game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T21:34:00-08:00","id":1355582,"title":"","content":"The problem with the rage mechanic using the ' Hunger/Murder' mechanic is the utterly random nature of it. Where as currently you know how angry your PC is with a V5 type mechanic you can lose your entire family and be unaffected or stub your toe and fall into Thrall....It's just not a good mechanic for long term play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T23:31:16-08:00","id":1355591,"title":"","content":"For WtA characters with Rage 4+, there was already a random chance that any stressful situation could send them flipping out. I've seen a Rage 6 Ahroun on a full moon, fail to frenzy (which is difficulty 3) when their kinfolk mate was killed, and a Philodox that was temp. Rage 4 Frenzy on a cub that was being a pain in the ass about Garou law.<br /> <br /> You can say it's not a good mechanic for long term play... but it's not really that far from how WtA already works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T00:11:44-08:00","id":1355592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355591#post1355591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For WtA characters with Rage 4+, there was already a random chance that any stressful situation could send them flipping out. I've seen a Rage 6 Ahroun on a full moon, fail to frenzy (which is difficulty 3) when their kinfolk mate was killed, and a Philodox that was temp. Rage 4 Frenzy on a cub that was being a pain in the ass about Garou law.<br /> <br /> You can say it's not a good mechanic for long term play... but it's not really that far from how WtA already works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If it you run the numbers and it functions the same as V5 you'll find it is very different indeed. Especially with how the reduced Willpower plays into it, every single Garou interaction is going to have a very good chance of turning into a bloodbath at the drop of a hat....hell, packs are going to have a hell of a time even functioning.<br /> <br /> Of course, you can always just 'take half' for every single action but that reduces the game to a slog where you play Garou that will never achieve anything of note.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T00:27:42-08:00","id":1355594,"title":"","content":"That's fairly dependent on what the results of Rage would be. I'm not saying it would work copied from V5 directly, but that the general setup is something that can actually work with Rage as Rage is describe in the books.<br /> <br /> If rolling a Messy Crit in W5 turns into a Frenzy? Sure, that's bad, but that's not how V5 works. If a Messy Crit in W5 reflects things like The Beast Within where Garou suffer social penalties from their Rage? That works just fine without things falling into a blood bath.<br /> <br /> I know the V5 numbers just fine, but I know the WtA math just fine too. If you follow the current WtA RAW, Rage 4+ Garou are already Frenzy machines because they can't regain WP nearly fast enough to keep their Frenzies in check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T00:49:12-08:00","id":1355597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355594#post1355594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fairly dependent on what the results of Rage would be. I'm not saying it would work copied from V5 directly, but that the general setup is something that can actually work with Rage as Rage is describe in the books.<br /> <br /> If rolling a Messy Crit in W5 turns into a Frenzy? Sure, that's bad, but that's not how V5 works. If a Messy Crit in W5 reflects things like The Beast Within where Garou suffer social penalties from their Rage? That works just fine without things falling into a blood bath.<br /> <br /> I know the V5 numbers just fine, but I know the WtA math just fine too. If you follow the current WtA RAW, Rage 4+ Garou are already Frenzy machines because they can't regain WP nearly fast enough to keep their Frenzies in check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.....I mean normally your pretty spot on but I've played V5 ( 2 months before giving up) and I've been playing WtA since 93 and the occurences of Frenzy and &quot;Masquerade/Veil&quot; breaches in V5 are an order of magnitude higher than in the average WtA game for the same number of rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T01:01:10-08:00","id":1355598,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how you get that unless you make every Messy Crit/Bestial failure in V5 count as a Frenzy or breach.<br /> <br /> They're certainly far too frequent for my tastes, but vampires aren't supposed to get snarly and nasty in an off putting fashion just by walking around. The majority of werewolves can't walk around humans without magic powers hiding their natures, and not have Rage get in the way.<br /> <br /> Full Frenzies in WtA IME are quite common, but maybe we tend to play rougher combat scenes where Frenzy happen a lot and save your life for it than average.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T07:43:45-08:00","id":1355635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355598#post1355598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Full Frenzies in WtA IME are quite common, but maybe we tend to play rougher combat scenes where Frenzy happen a lot and save your life for it than average.</div> </div> </div> </div>To an amount that they hinder the game and aren't an element of horror anymore, but a recurring break in the plot for a time consuming combat intermezzo.<br /> <br /> Really, anyone ever tried to storytell a Moot, which has to happen at full moon according to the setting, and have one frenzy trigger...? Game session is done, unless one changes the rules or forbids players to roll for frenzy every time they think their character is insulted, or worried, or has any strong emotion....for they are all triggers.<br /> <br /> Hell, according to the rules all tribes should have wiped themselves out, except for the Get of Fenris, who can use a Rite to raise difficulties of Rage rolls to 9 during Moots.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T09:49:47-08:00","id":1355649,"title":"","content":"Also that.<br /> <br /> Though Moots can be mitigated a bit without house rules. Higher Rank Garou have bonuses to resist Frenzy, and most groups I play in rarely have PCs raise perm. Rage over 3 unless forced by Auspice until the game gets up in Rank for those boosts. So with 3/5 of the younger Garou unable to Frenzy even with rolling all successes (though I perceive how that works in the RAW to be a flaw in its own right as Rage 1 should still have some Frenzy risk without having to allow Rage to accumulate to 4 temp. first), most of the leadership that aren't still low-ish Rage having an easier time not Frenzying, and making sure you have people around with a few select Gifts to halt Frenzies... you can run a Moot without it falling apart. Though Renown loss because the dice hate you is a bit too common (and screws Galliards the hardest).<br /> <br /> Of course, it's extremely forced to have every functional Sept have a nearly identical setup because it's the only way to make Moots work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T10:42:06-08:00","id":1355657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355635#post1355635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To an amount that they hinder the game and aren't an element of horror anymore, but a recurring break in the plot for a time consuming combat intermezzo.</div> </div> </div> </div>*character frenzies, freeze frame effect*<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jn-KkqQOres\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;We'll be right back!&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, anyone ever tried to storytell a Moot, which has to happen at full moon according to the setting, and have one frenzy trigger...? Game session is done, unless one changes the rules or forbids players to roll for frenzy every time they think their character is insulted, or worried, or has any strong emotion....for they are all triggers.<br /> <br /> Hell, according to the rules all tribes should have wiped themselves out, except for the Get of Fenris, who can use a Rite to raise difficulties of Rage rolls to 9 during Moots. </div> </div> </div>Particularly accomplished Shadow Lords of the Bringers of Light can also send their successes needed to frenzy up to 10 as a permanent, passive effect. This is only a reward via a particular celebratory rite, though (8+ successes needed to frenzy as on option on the Rite of Conquest, on top of the bonus from high Rank), so it's rare that anyone will have it. At any rate, if the Garou moots are bloodbaths waiting to happen, Rokea gatherings are probably avoided by all concerned weresharks because they ended up screwed over by the &quot;Jaws&quot; image, saddled with only two successes necessary to frenzy.<br /> <br /> Then we also have to differentiate between berserk frenzy and fox frenzy. So it's clear that even as things are, there's probably a need for a new system, but Hunger was made for a very different purpose, and isn't going to give a clear picture of building up steam, or differentiating between the fight and flight explosions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T11:35:11-08:00","id":1355666,"title":"","content":"didn't W20 make it so that nothing but combat could make Garou frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T14:08:24-08:00","id":1355694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355657#post1355657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then we also have to differentiate between berserk frenzy and fox frenzy. So it's clear that even as things are, there's probably a need for a new system, but Hunger was made for a very different purpose, and isn't going to give a clear picture of building up steam, or differentiating between the fight and flight explosions.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunger framework doesn't replace having specific Frenzy mechanics. V5 has the VtM equivalents to this as their own thing. V5's Hunger mechanics can provoke Frenzies (and has a specific Hunger Frenzy as well that's worse the higher your Hunger), but you can Frenzy outside of Hunger and there's already fight and flight Frenzies there.<br /> <br /> For all that I don't like how Hunger works, replicating how WtA operates in this regard is not hard with the V5 base concepts. If you want to keep arguing contrary to this, it would be nice if you stepped up your game a bit in demonstrating why you think it wouldn't work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355666#post1355666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">didn't W20 make it so that nothing but combat could make Garou frenzy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the slightest. W20 p. 261-262 list a number of potential reasons to roll Rage for a Frenzy, none of which are combat specific. And you can explicitly Frenzy in situations such as using your Rage in place of your standard dice in a stare down contest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T15:37:23-08:00","id":1355702,"title":"","content":"I must be thinking of Forsaken then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T15:59:43-08:00","id":1355707,"title":"","content":"Um, still very much not true in either edition of Forsaken. In Forsaken 2e, it's a Death Rage trigger to take the war-form <i>outside</i> of combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T17:18:49-08:00","id":1355724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355694#post1355694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Hunger framework doesn't replace having specific Frenzy mechanics. V5 has the VtM equivalents to this as their own thing. V5's Hunger mechanics can provoke Frenzies (and has a specific Hunger Frenzy as well that's worse the higher your Hunger), but you can Frenzy outside of Hunger and there's already fight and flight Frenzies there.<br /> <br /> For all that I don't like how Hunger works, replicating how WtA operates in this regard is not hard with the V5 base concepts. If you want to keep arguing contrary to this, it would be nice if you stepped up your game a bit in demonstrating why you think it wouldn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Ananasi will presumably work like vampires in terms of blood use, as they have previously. They are supposed to be unusual in working like this, an oddity compared to Garou and other Fera. Hence, Rage should not be similar to Hunger, because that would make Ananasi function too much like the Ovid, and that's contrary to the design goals of Ananasi.<br /> <br /> This is, you know, in addition to Rage never having functioned on a voluntary increase basis, which you keep brushing off as unimportant. This feels similar to Vampires from the prior system losing blood points the first time that they looked at the moon each night, or if they became humiliated, presumably because in becoming upset they began gushing out waterfalls of crimson tears like they were in a shoujo manga.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T18:09:53-08:00","id":1355734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355724#post1355724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ananasi will presumably work like vampires in terms of blood use, as they have previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows? That's a pretty long way away. You're also stretching really damned far, again. How will werespiders work wasn't a design priority of any WtA corebook ever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are supposed to be unusual in working like this, an oddity compared to Garou and other Fera. </div> </div> </div>O..K... Then (probably for the worse) the Ananasi will probably have actual V5 Hunger, while Garou and other Fera with Rage will have W5 Hunger-like Rage. And they will be an oddity again.<br /> <br /> Rage and Blood were both &quot;here's a pool of points to spend on powers,&quot; as very similar mechanics. What makes Ananasi blood so strange are what they can spend it on. If they spent it on all the same things as Rage is used for it wouldn't feel all that distinct.<br /> <br /> That's what you're constantly ignoring in all this. The specifics of Rage in W5 is going to be different from Hunger in V5 (we can only presume). Instead of just acknowledging that just like vitae could be gained and spent on powers like Rage can be gained and spent on powers, while still being wildly different in how that plays out, so Hunger and W5 Rage can do the same thing, you're trying to obscure this all behind various nonsensical statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is, you know, in addition to Rage never having functioned on a voluntary increase basis, which you keep brushing off as unimportant. </div> </div> </div>Because &quot;voluntary&quot; is a fairly meaningless thing. Seeing the moon for the first time in the night is a voluntary action. Interacting with people that might try to piss you off is a voluntary action. Being ambushed with silver is an involuntary situation. Rage isn't one way or the other.<br /> <br /> The base mechanical design of Hunger in V5 is a mix of voluntary and involuntary increases in Hunger. That can be replicated.<br /> <br /> And I'm not brushing it off as unimportant, but rather WtA as it stands now is actually counter-thematic with how Rage works. Stoking Rage for power making it harder to control yourself makes more sense than tearing into a bunch of fomori to calm down. Getting rid of Rage is too easy in WtA as it stands. The mechanics of things like the Curse and Beast Within are too easily forgotten when they're supposed to be important complications. Have Rage that is hard to decrease in the moment and builds up instead of drains actually explores &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot; by making unleashing Rage inevitable, instead of, &quot;I go to the bathroom and shift to Glabro with Rage and back a few times until I've shed my excess Rage and now I can't Frenzy.&quot; And yes, that's a thing in way too many WtA games I've been in &quot;excusing one's self,&quot; is shorthand for, &quot;go find a away to burn temp. Rage to equal to perm. Rage.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T19:05:12-08:00","id":1355741,"title":"","content":"Um...Rage is anger, primal anger but still anger. Of course your going to feel less angry after giving that rage an outlet, the same way sparring or a heavy gym session drains tension away.<br /> <br /> Never had ' excusing oneself' be a thing ever but YGMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 12-18-2019, 10:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T20:04:25-08:00","id":1355748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355734#post1355734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who knows? That's a pretty long way away. You're also stretching really damned far, again. How will werespiders work wasn't a design priority of any WtA corebook ever.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> O..K... Then (probably for the worse) the Ananasi will probably have actual V5 Hunger, while Garou and other Fera with Rage will have W5 Hunger-like Rage. And they will be an oddity again.<br /> <br /> Rage and Blood were both &quot;here's a pool of points to spend on powers,&quot; as very similar mechanics. What makes Ananasi blood so strange are what they can spend it on. If they spent it on all the same things as Rage is used for it wouldn't feel all that distinct.<br /> <br /> That's what you're constantly ignoring in all this. The specifics of Rage in W5 is going to be different from Hunger in V5 (we can only presume). Instead of just acknowledging that just like vitae could be gained and spent on powers like Rage can be gained and spent on powers, while still being wildly different in how that plays out, so Hunger and W5 Rage can do the same thing, you're trying to obscure this all behind various nonsensical statements.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Because &quot;voluntary&quot; is a fairly meaningless thing. Seeing the moon for the first time in the night is a voluntary action. Interacting with people that might try to piss you off is a voluntary action. Being ambushed with silver is an involuntary situation. Rage isn't one way or the other.<br /> <br /> The base mechanical design of Hunger in V5 is a mix of voluntary and involuntary increases in Hunger. That can be replicated.<br /> <br /> And I'm not brushing it off as unimportant, but rather WtA as it stands now is actually counter-thematic with how Rage works. Stoking Rage for power making it harder to control yourself makes more sense than tearing into a bunch of fomori to calm down. Getting rid of Rage is too easy in WtA as it stands. The mechanics of things like the Curse and Beast Within are too easily forgotten when they're supposed to be important complications. Have Rage that is hard to decrease in the moment and builds up instead of drains actually explores &quot;When Will You Rage?&quot; by making unleashing Rage inevitable, instead of, &quot;I go to the bathroom and shift to Glabro with Rage and back a few times until I've shed my excess Rage and now I can't Frenzy.&quot; And yes, that's a thing in way too many WtA games I've been in &quot;excusing one's self,&quot; is shorthand for, &quot;go find a away to burn temp. Rage to equal to perm. Rage.&quot;<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, that last point? You're going off on me because of a failure of your own house rules. There are riders that are supposed to permit Rage use only under times of stress; merely having Rage won't permit you to just burn it off, especially not in the rare, typically inescapable situations where temporary exceeds permanent. The bit about just going off somewhere to burn off Rage is also very similar to the off-screen hunting style occasionally used in Vampire. No wonder you don't see a problem with using Hunger for Rage; you completely ignored how it was supposed to work and then took a page from V:tM to step even further around its consequences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T22:32:08-08:00","id":1355771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355748#post1355748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, that last point? You're going off on me because of a failure of your own house rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, my house rules have long since removed these things as being issues actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are riders that are supposed to permit Rage use only under times of stress; </div> </div> </div>Having temp. Rage &gt; perm. Rage is inherently a time of stress. As you yourself point out that this is only supposed to happen under significant strain in the first place. &quot;If I don't get myself under control, I'm going to screw up this important and delicate negotiations between some Get and Wendigo,&quot; is both more than RAW justification to have a Philodox bump up to temp. Rage 4, and be under enough stress to qualify for the rider one spending Rage.<br /> <br /> The rider is, effectively, pointless. Stress generates Rage, so any time you'd want to spend Rage just for the sake of doing so you're going to be under stress.<br /> <br /> Where the rider in question really comes into play are things like trying to use extra actions or Rage activated Gifts in calm situations, which frequently just makes a lot of Gifts underwhelming if they require Rage but are still mostly utility effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The bit about just going off somewhere to burn off Rage is also very similar to the off-screen hunting style occasionally used in Vampire. </div> </div> </div>No, its not.<br /> <br /> 1) It's generally much faster. It's going off for a few moments, not an hour or so.<br /> <br /> 2) It's not a group downtime issue. It's not, &quot;OK, what are people doing before the scene starts, including feeding?&quot; It's actively removing a PC from the scene for what could be a vital minute. It's far more comparable to on-screen feeding where one vampire is particularly low on vitae and opts to find some food now instead of wait for off-screen feeding time later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No wonder you don't see a problem with using Hunger for Rage; you completely ignored how it was supposed to work and then took a page from V:tM to step even further around its consequences. </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, I know what I'm talking about and you're stuck misrepresenting things because you have no leg to stand on with this.<br /> <br /> You still haven't actually backed up all sorts of assertions you've made, and your attempts to just poke holes in my posts are pathetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T00:15:23-08:00","id":1355785,"title":"","content":"I never understood the mechanical point of Camps, as there were none when I was reading through any book. Think they'll add em in this edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:09:24-08:00","id":1355792,"title":"","content":"Camps are meant to mostly be a social faction sort of thing, though many have a few Gifts you can get at in-Tribe costs (some of which are supposed to be rare or unique to those Camps).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:19:10-08:00","id":1355795,"title":"","content":"W5 probably will have camps, for there is no reasonable way to explain them away. Mechanical the don't make to much sense, and I always rule that their camp gifts are foreign gifts for they shall not be a way to get another set of cheap gifts. Setting wise the are introduced in Player's Guides and Tribe Books and basically serve as groups of like minded garou within a tribe, possibly with some goal or duty they gave themselves. It might have been a design flaw to not make some camps inter-tribal to begin with, but that is another topic. Possibly W5 will change that and state that it has been a development of the last decade. Hopefully with a sidebar stating &quot;Could have been intertribal since the camp formed, if you like&quot;. But I surely hope they don't shove retcons down our throat, like W20 did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T01:21:26-08:00","id":1355796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355792#post1355792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Camps are meant to mostly be a social faction sort of thing, though many have a few Gifts you can get at in-Tribe costs (some of which are supposed to be rare or unique to those Camps).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, most TBs have gifts of camps listed as camp gifts. TB BG rev has some gifts that are pretty obviously designed for a camp mentioned in the TB, but the gifts section doesn't divide by camps, so BG just have a huge amout of tribal-gifts from their tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T13:47:17-08:00","id":1355934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355771#post1355771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, my house rules have long since removed these things as being issues actually.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad, and yet not my bad. The problem is the Revised core, which didn't include the 2nd edition header in the Drama chapter, &quot;Stress&quot;, page 211. That was a vital mistake, and if you had been playing in an older game, none of what you described would have been encouraged or even allowed behavior.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having temp. Rage &gt; perm. Rage is inherently a time of stress. As you yourself point out that this is only supposed to happen under significant strain in the first place. &quot;If I don't get myself under control, I'm going to screw up this important and delicate negotiations between some Get and Wendigo,&quot; is both more than RAW justification to have a Philodox bump up to temp. Rage 4, and be under enough stress to qualify for the rider one spending Rage. </div> </div> </div>If you have your character thinking clearly about the situation, it seems that you might not be roleplaying the extremely strained state of mind correctly. It would also be highly appropriate to roll for frenzy before allowing any other decisions on the part of the player, as well as restrict just what outlets were viable for Rage. That's part of an ST's discretion to avoid undercutting the themes of the game, and it wouldn't even come to the ST's explicit ruling if W:tA Revised had maintained some semblance of 2e's guidelines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rider is, effectively, pointless. Stress generates Rage, so any time you'd want to spend Rage just for the sake of doing so you're going to be under stress.<br /> <br /> Where the rider in question really comes into play are things like trying to use extra actions or Rage activated Gifts in calm situations, which frequently just makes a lot of Gifts underwhelming if they require Rage but are still mostly utility effects. </div> </div> </div>Here's what the missing pieces from 2e have to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Werewolf 2nd Edition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stress<br /> <br /> Stress is an important consideration for werewolves. Garou cannot use Rage to gain extra actions unless they are under stress. On the other hand, too much stress can push a Garou right over the edge, sending him into a frenzy. [... outlining familiar rules for how to frenzy cut]<br /> <br /> So what is stress? Stress is any situation that causes tension in a character. Any time a character begins to feel edgy, threatened, or confused may qualify as a stressful situation. The following are examples:<br /> Combat, Impending Danger, Confusion, Unexpected Happening, Frustration (as in disarming a bomb, not typical actions), Storyteller's Discretion. [note: each has a longer description, omitted for brevity]<br /> <br /> Make sure that you, as the Storyteller, don't cheat your players out of stressful situations. Any combat scene is stressful, and most action scenes as well. There is nothing more frustrating to players than not being able to use their characters' special abilities (Rage), and nothing makings players leave games faster than frustration. This is not to say that you should always let players convince you into ruling that a scene is stressful. Just try to balance things out and use common sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, no, you aren't supposed to be able to just go off and burn Rage safely, regardless of whether or not you happen to think that &quot;Stress&quot; is too open a term for danger and uncertainty or the Revised core forgot to tell you something important. That's pretty clearly antithetical to the dramatic nature of Rage expressed in this passage. If your ST was allowing it otherwise, that was very much against the spirit of the setting and mechanics, even if it got lost in the shuffle across editions. More's the pity; it seems like it could have salvaged those games that got ruined for you, or at least helped avoid loophole abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T15:26:41-08:00","id":1355956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355934#post1355934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My bad, and yet not my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>No Just your bad. You're still wrong even quoting 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was a vital mistake... </div> </div> </div>Or Revise and W20 (which both don't have that) felt that the words wasted on it were just that, a waste. Stress is still a broad concept and spending that much word count on it doesn't really add anything to the game. It just spends a lot of time coming up with different ways to say, &quot;this is a potentially stressful situation.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..., and if you had been playing in an older game, none of what you described would have been encouraged or even allowed behavior. </div> </div> </div>I've been playing since 2e thank you, and you're wrong in an incredibly obnoxious way:<br /> <br /> Because all of that stuff in 2e? It doesn't stop you from spending Rage to avoid having too much temporary Rage if the situation is stressful enough to cause that state in the first place.<br /> <br /> Lacking, &quot;this is an exhaustive list of stressful situations,&quot; it doesn't change anything. That passage actually formed my old groups feelings that the &quot;only spend Rage under stress,&quot; thing was silly, since again, the vast majority of time you're going to want to spend Rage, the situation is stressful under those guidelines. They're incredibly broad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have your character thinking clearly about the situation, it seems that you might not be roleplaying the extremely strained state of mind correctly. </div> </div> </div>So, your best argument here is to insult my role-playing? Not exactly convincing that you have one iota of a point in your favor here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would also be highly appropriate to roll for frenzy before allowing any other decisions on the part of the player, as well as restrict just what outlets were viable for Rage. </div> </div> </div>Always options however:<br /> <br /> 1) The ST might not really want a Frenzy fucking with the plot in that moment.<br /> <br /> 2) The group might not want the ST to be too heavy handed with these things considering the rather high potential for catastrophic results. Nobody likes it when the game results in TPKs too often, especially if the ST keeps forcing things that way.<br /> <br /> If the ST has to manipulate the situation to make deny this possibility, than you're admitting it's not actually my groups being shitty readers and shitty role-players for actually paying attention to what the books say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, no, you aren't supposed to be able to just go off and burn Rage safely,... </div> </div> </div>Please highlight what line in that passage actually supports that.<br /> <br /> &quot;So what is stress? Stress is any situation that causes tension in a character.&quot; Well, that's an extremely broad statement.<br /> <br /> &quot;Any time a character begins to feel edgy, threatened, or confused may qualify as a stressful situation.&quot; That didn't narrow anything down. Those are just various forms of tension.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is nothing more frustrating to players than not being able to use their characters' special abilities (Rage), and nothing makings players leave games faster than frustration.&quot; So, the game is saying to not be too heavy-handed. Don't be overly restrictive with what counts as stress; it's mean to be extremely open. Also, don't frustrate your players. You know what's frustrating? Constantly having to clean up after Frenzies.<br /> <br /> Not stated? That you can't use Rage in a stressful situation to reduce your temp. Rage on purpose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's pretty clearly antithetical to the dramatic nature of Rage expressed in this passage. </div> </div> </div>Not really, &quot;On the other hand, too much stress can push a Garou right over the edge, sending him into a frenzy.&quot; means that the dramatic nature of Rage, as expressed, is that Garou will look for way to decrease stress because Frenzy is bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your ST was allowing it otherwise, that was very much against the spirit of the setting and mechanics, even if it got lost in the shuffle across editions. </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. It's very much against the bad faith, obviously made up to avoid having to admit you're wrong here, interpretation you're insisting is the One True Way, even though the interpretation you're citing is clearly not supported in the books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T17:18:03-08:00","id":1355968,"title":"","content":"Personally im of the mindset that Garou can &quot;cool off&quot; their temp. rage. They just don't because. Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11112-brothermouse","name":"BrotherMouse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11112_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T17:48:09-08:00","id":1355974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrotherMouse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1355968#post1355968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally im of the mindset that Garou can &quot;cool off&quot; their temp. rage. They just don't because. Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just had my character spend excess rage by shadow boxing. But I think the mechanics were that you'd always roll the Highest of your temp/permanent rage, so there was no point in burning more than my permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-19T18:10:46-08:00","id":1355978,"title":"","content":"The only point in dropping your temp. Rage further is if there's a predictable source of temp. Rage coming.<br /> <br /> If your PC has screwed up, and knows they're in for a humiliating Moot as the Philodoxes are about to make an example of you, while the Ragabash sharpen their tongues, and you know the Galliards are working on how to turn your shame into stories to warn future generations? Drop your temp. Rage as low as you can, so it doesn't get pushed up over perm. during your time to endure your punishment. You're going to want some more room to eat up the temp. Rage you'll be getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T07:34:14-08:00","id":1356089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1354873#post1354873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Failure doesn't meen total war.<br /> <br /> Yesterday I've walked a lot and tried to figure out how could all the tribe failed.<br /> <br /> Generaly: Gaia isn't saved, the ecosystem is crumbling, spiececs die out day to day. Caerns loose they potency, maybe even the Fera starts to loose their spiritual Potency.<br /> Less and less Garou are born, Metis is the main Breed. They are breed as needed shock-troops.<br /> The Veil was shattered. The Second Inquisition started to hunt Garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Furies:</b> Less and less wild placecs remain. Women are still used, abused, threw, and Wyrm uses bigotry on BOTH sides to foster hatred. They number dwindled, and had to accept men into their rank. They identity is shattered<br /> <b>Bone Gnawers:</b> Died out. Lone survivors remain, but the tribe is no more.<br /> <b>Children of Gaia:</b> There is no peace. The Nation is fragmented. But there were successfull. They brought back the Bunyip, or something wearing their skin. They live, breed and figh. The Third War of Rage is brewing in Australia, but now the Garou are on the loosing side.<br /> <b>Fianna:</b> No more boose? Donno. Because of the almost forgotten ties to the Good Folk, Tallain become very intrested in them. Now they are hunted by nightmares and loose ancecstral land to them and the Spirals.<br /> <b>Get of Fenris:</b> There is no epic war to figh. What's their purose now?<br /> <b>Glas Walkers:</b> Technology become a weakness. Men adapted faster, now the system is used against them. The Weaver becomes stronger, the webs thicker. Some of them even started to fall.<br /> <b>Red Talons:</b> Wolves die out. A new Impergium was started and it failed. Human technology was stronger. Drones are unaffected by the Delirium, Hellfire Missiles burns Caerns and meet. The Second Inquisition started to hunt the changers, not just vampires.<br /> <b>Silver Fangs:</b> Heroes die. Fangs lost their power, their blood is diluted. They lost the Crown and influence. No one trusts a fallen leader.<br /> <b>Shadow Lords:</b> Couldn't grab the power. Tried, fought, tore down the Fangs, but what they could achieve is a fragmented Nation. Tribes and Camps without guadiance and leadership.<br /> Silent Striders: Could not break the Curse. Wepauvet was able to connect some Ancestors with newborns, but later other spirits, things used the connections. Nowdays the youth of the tribe is the playground of wraiths.<br /> Stargazers: Tribal homeland was lost, and the Beast Court doesn't accepted them as it was expected. Now they are outcasts.<br /> <b>Uktena:</b> Banes gets free, Storm Eater is aproaching.<br /> <b>Wendigo:</b> The natives are constantly used, abused. More and more Kin is lost to mixed pairing and Wendigo looses it's spiritual &quot;purity&quot;. It's getting more tainted and cannibalism is occuring in alarming frequency.<br /> <br /> Bonus:<br /> <br /> <b>BSDs:</b> Wyrm is not free, Weaver is stronger every day. The Metis population is so high that tht Tribe may die out / weaken in one generation. They are in the focus of Second Inquisition.</div> </div> </div> </div>and radical war in 2020 doesn't necessary mean a all out phyical war <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Nice suggestions about the tribes. Really similar to what I described in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T15:50:27-08:00","id":1356187,"title":"","content":"Here's how I'd end the tribes.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: Are now nominally a tribe; They have given up and act as though they are ronin, with no purpose in the war. Second, much cooler option; They join the Ratkin in war.<br /> Black Furies: The tribe was never great at breeding given they deny themselves men. New feminists are turned off by the tribes hatred for trans people, whilst the mainstream sees feminism becoming 'toxic' and the tribe has become marginalized.<br /> Children of Gaia: Self indulgent virtue signaling and the agressive drive to become 'PC' among neoliberal circles has completely undermined the tribe. Just as America voted trump in a backlash, so too does everyone spurn the CoG<br /> Fianna- Universal harrano.<br /> Get of Fenrir- Fighting their way to extinction.<br /> Glass walkers- Weaver took em.<br /> Silver Fangs- Inbreeding<br /> Silent striders- Having lost hope of reclaiming their ancestral homelands, the silent striders disband.<br /> Shadow lords- The Wyrm got to them, or the other tribes think the Wyrm has got to them.<br /> Stargazers- Left for the deep umbra, never to return. <br /> Red Talons: Human kin were exterminated without them noticing. As a result the tribe can no longer breed true.<br /> Uktenka- Same as shadow lords<br /> Wendigo- Warred with the other garou; Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T13:48:50-08:00","id":1357880,"title":"","content":"Above you went into a small (, but significant) part of the system. A system we know almost nothing.<br /> <br /> I'd be more intrested in the story / background. If it's fine with a horrendous system it still could be played with the old one.<br /> But if the system is the best, but the fluff is bad it could kill the whole gemeline.<br /> <br /> I'm familiar with V5. The background was a joke. Second Inquisition? Really? Like a bad live thread went official.<br /> <br /> I hope W5 will be handled better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-04T00:53:50-08:00","id":1358780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1357880#post1357880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm familiar with V5. The background was a joke. Second Inquisition? Really? Like a bad live thread went official.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I mean making something like.. the Masquerade matter is kind of silly. I know. I mean it shouldn't be a key feature rather than over the top blood gods being untouchable by humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member"