avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T19:30:57-08:00","id":1360626,"title":"","content":"I wanted people to be happy about it when I created this thread gdang it. A brand new edition of werewolf the apocalypse! What is so wrong with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T21:52:02-08:00","id":1360640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360617#post1360617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heavy,how can w5 criticism be legitimate. If w5 is not written yt?</div> </div> </div> </div>People are criticizing the promotional materials, Paradox's licensing decisions, and so on.<br /> <br /> They're negatively speculating based on V5 what W5 will likely be forced to include by Paradox to keep a consistent mechanical and thematic tone with V5 as a unified WoD set of games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360618#post1360618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've heard the white wolf personnel,called monsters,idiots,dumbasses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard lots of people say nasty things about lots of other people.<br /> <br /> If you cared about the tone of the conversation, you'd care about what actual, real people, here are saying. Not whatever the worst things you've every heard people say on a topic regardless of it not being part of this conversation.<br /> <br /> I've been called all sorts of shitty things for expressing my opinions about V5... never seen you give a shit about it. It can't be a one sided thing. If all you're trying to do is stan of the Paradox crew? It's not going to help anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've heard that they dont know what they doing. </div> </div> </div>They made considerable mistakes with the properties so far. Assuming they didn't really know what they were doing is the <u>nice</u> option. It's far better than assuming they did these things purposefully knowing they were bad choices.<br /> <br /> Would you rather we assume they're people that tired to do their best and failed to live up to their own stated standards let alone our personal standards? Or people that did exactly what they were trying to do, and all the bad stuff was precisely what they wanted it to be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've talked to them yknow? </div> </div> </div>I've corresponded with some of them as well. The were polite to me, but I wouldn't really say kind. I'd mostly say politely bland corporate speak that didn't really make me feel listen to as opposed to letting them check off that they answered a customer complaint.<br /> <br /> They made decisions that were obviously going to upset people. They made those decisions despite people trying to warn them not to. That doesn't mean every name they've been called is justified, but it's hardly this one-sided or out-of-the-blue situation you're making it out to be. <br /> <br /> And lets put this in perspective. What they've been subjected to is a light slap on the face compared to what the Internet can dish out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360619#post1360619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,I gotta say I'm disappointed with the admins not banning brothermouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you want everyone that doesn't agree with your feelings about this stuff banned? Because a lot of us have said the same, if not worse, as brothermouse. Like I said, it feels like you care more about silencing one side than really deeply caring about the larger tone of the conversation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360624#post1360624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Martin was accused or locking a claustrophobic person in a locker when they were both 17. The guy said on FB a few months ago it was just roleplaying. It was consensual that whats I meant</div> </div> </div> </div>While this story might have been exaggerated upon retelling (which is partly Martin's fault considering the way he has talked about it publicly, but Martin really needs to have a native English speaker check his phrasing before he says serious stuff in general), what you're saying doesn't actually say what you think.<br /> <br /> &quot;It was consensual,&quot; just acknowledges that it happened. There's a lot of things that people find distasteful even if done by consenting individuals. Seventeen year olds shouldn't be performing exposure therapy even if it's consensual any more than seventeen year olds should be performing surgeries even if it's consensual. LARP runners shouldn't be allowing their games to be used for that sort of thing by amateurs either. Both combined is even worse.<br /> <br /> So even the best interpretation of events is still bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360625#post1360625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's criticizing a game that it's not ready yet! Hes saying a game that is not written is bad!</div> </div> </div> </div>He's stating his lack of confidence in the game turning out well. It's not the same as what you're accusing him of. His concerns that it will turn out bad are as valid as your hope it turns out well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360626#post1360626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted people to be happy about it when I created this thread gdang it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... it really shouldn't have been hard to tell that the WoD 5e stuff is not something to start threads about if you want to just have happy feel discussions.<br /> <br /> Also, you didn't actually do anything to guide this thread in a specific direction. You posted a tweet for people to respond to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T21:55:52-08:00","id":1360641,"title":"","content":"So. Ive posted an apology here <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1360632-i-m-sorry\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...0632-i-m-sorry</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T16:29:28-08:00","id":1360784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360570#post1360570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's nothing quite as lazy as dismissing negativity as fear mongering.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not lazy and fear mongering is exactly what it is. Y\u2019all are rousing each other up by imagining how terrible it can be instead of taking an alternative route and wondering about how good it could be. <br /> <br /> Now if it comes out and it\u2019s trash yeah I\u2019ll own up to being wrong, but it isn\u2019t out yet and for all we know the design team could be long time werewolf fans who respect the lore. Putting the horse before the carriage. <br /> <br /> Also did not know changing ways was edited before release. That\u2019s terrible for the writers who worked on the elements of the book that were good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T18:13:17-08:00","id":1360795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360784#post1360784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s not lazy and fear mongering is exactly what it is. Y\u2019all are rousing each other up by imagining how terrible it can be instead of taking an alternative route and wondering about how good it could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's exceedingly lazy.<br /> <br /> It's lazy because you're treating a group of people as a hivemind so that you don't have to deal with the nuance of each individual's actual thoughts, feelings, and positions.<br /> <br /> It's lazy because you're using a label to avoid having to engage with actual posts where you'd have to do more than use a label like it was a magic wand to make it go away.<br /> <br /> It's lazy because you're committing the same sort of hypocrisy as Nicolas just apologized for where you're forced to argue that people pessimistic about W5 should have their ability to post about W5 curtained so others don't have to exert energy addressing issues they raise.<br /> <br /> It's also not fearmongering, because fearmongering is an active attempt to whip up fear and panic to a general population to mislead their decision making.<br /> <br /> It's not fearmongering if we can, as we have, articulate a reasonable basis for our fears about the future of WtA.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, get off your high horse.<br /> <br /> Also? I'm under no obligation to imagine W5 in any specific light. Considering my opinions of the factual on the record thing that is V5's base system, I can't imagine W5 being what I would call &quot;good&quot; as it is, because the foundations would be the same foundations I don't think are of that quality. Even so, despite your vapid accusations, I spent multiple posts in this thread <b>defending</b> V5's Hunger mechanics (which I highly dislike) as something that could be salvaged for Rage in W5. Because you're, yes lazy, statements show you're not really paying attention to anything other than reasons to tone police.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now if it comes out and it\u2019s trash yeah I\u2019ll own up to being wrong,... </div> </div> </div>Of course, you never have to, because you can defend whatever it is, no matter how it ends up, as good to you. If you want to say something like this that has some meaning to it, give some metrics we can actually hold you to account for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but it isn\u2019t out yet and for all we know the design team could be long time werewolf fans who respect the lore. </div> </div> </div>These two ideas have no logical connection.<br /> <br /> So what if they are? The V5 team was made up of long time VtM fans who believe they respect the lore, and respected the lore with V5; however I feel about that. Being fans of the game, doesn't mean anything for predicting the product they'll turn out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T23:26:03-08:00","id":1360825,"title":"","content":"So, any news, leaks or some other infos about upcoming stuff?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T06:59:01-08:00","id":1360872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360619#post1360619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also,I gotta say I'm disappointed with the admins not banning brothermouse.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>If you have a problem with another user's conduct you need to hit that report button. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-14T08:43:14-08:00","id":1360890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360784#post1360784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not lazy and fear mongering is exactly what it is. Y\u2019all are rousing each other up by imagining how terrible it can be instead of taking an alternative route and wondering about how good it could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not fear mongering to say &quot;this other thing the company put out was subjectively bad, these other things the company forced changes on was subjectively bad, and since that is all I have available regarding the company's handling of the game, I worry this new thing will also be subjectively bad&quot;. That is simple extrapolation.<br /> <br /> Fear mongering would be saying &quot;nWW's handling of the WoD game licenses will make the entire WoD franchise poisoned, ruining it for the future and for all time&quot;. While there are people out there saying that (or similar stuff), it's not a prevalent theme in this thread. They are looking at V5, looking at nWW's statements, looking at the products for the WoD that nWW had altered, and they are making a judgement based on that previous behavior.<br /> <br /> It's not lazy to look at the past evidence and past behavior, to look at the current statements and see how they line up with that past behavior, and to then expect more of the same. That objectively takes more effort than to wave a hand at it all and say &quot;I'm sure it will all be fine, because I want it to be fine&quot;. Laziness is handwaving those concerns with a generalized label and upturned nose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T20:30:16-08:00","id":1361839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1360890#post1360890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is not fear mongering to say &amp;quot;this other thing the company put out was subjectively bad, these other things the company forced changes on was subjectively bad, and since that is all I have available regarding the company's handling of the game, I worry this new thing will also be subjectively bad&amp;quot;. That is simple extrapolation.<br /> <br /> Fear mongering would be saying &amp;quot;nWW's handling of the WoD game licenses will make the entire WoD franchise poisoned, ruining it for the future and for all time&amp;quot;. While there are people out there saying that (or similar stuff), it's not a prevalent theme in this thread. They are looking at V5, looking at nWW's statements, looking at the products for the WoD that nWW had altered, and they are making a judgement based on that previous behavior.<br /> <br /> It's not lazy to look at the past evidence and past behavior, to look at the current statements and see how they line up with that past behavior, and to then expect more of the same. That objectively takes more effort than to wave a hand at it all and say &amp;quot;I'm sure it will all be fine, because I want it to be fine&amp;quot;. Laziness is handwaving those concerns with a generalized label and upturned nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know where the hell you lot are deriving arrogance from on my part. The developer of w5 is a long time fan of werewolf who says (at least in the podcast) that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of werewolf while introducing new lore. It all sounded pretty good and frankly I\u2019m a little stoked. The whole crew dedicated themselves to getting this contract, and as fans I can\u2019t imagine they\u2019d want to bone it up. <br /> <br /> No what I\u2019ve seen from this thread is \u201cv5 is something I subjectively hate for x reason so w5 will be terrible because.\u201d It\u2019s about as bad as the warhammer fan base raging about every thing games workshop does (while weirdly defending their pricing which is predatory at best.). <br /> <br /> If anything I feel bad for the new devs since they\u2019re already set with the bar against them. That\u2019s stress they don\u2019t need. <br /> <br /> The podcast in question is the werewolf: the podcast. Give it a listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T23:24:50-08:00","id":1361860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361839#post1361839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u2019t know where the hell you lot are deriving arrogance from on my part. The developer of w5 is a long time fan of werewolf who says (at least in the podcast) that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of werewolf while introducing new lore. It all sounded pretty good and frankly I\u2019m a little stoked. The whole crew dedicated themselves to getting this contract, and as fans I can\u2019t imagine they\u2019d want to bone it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a longtime fan, were I to gain power over W5, I would drastically change a lot of things that have been getting under my skin for ages. A number of them are probably things that might not bother other people, or that others might actually have liked. Some of these might have even been central concepts; in my zeal to strike crossover from the integral structure of the game, for instance, I'd be at least sorely tempted to make drastic edits to the Silent Striders so that they spent too long around ghosts instead of being cursed by a borrowed, vampiric version of a Robert E. Howard character. I'm really tired of having to explain why the Metis breed is named the way it is in light of real world prejudices, and I'm not attached to the pseudeolatinate names of the others, so I would probably change them all, maybe even change the splat term &quot;Breed&quot; to something else like Birth, Origin, etc. Thrall of the Wyrm would be out (at least as a game term) in favor of Wits rolls for any frenzy to see if you chow down on a fallen enemy, like in 1e. If you're okay with Rage being measured in discrete states like the anima banner from Exalted 3rd edition, you wouldn't say that I boned it up, but if you were hoping for something closer to Hunger, well, it wouldn't be your lucky day if I ended up at the helm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T00:58:06-08:00","id":1361866,"title":"","content":"&quot;... a long time fan .........who says that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of ********** while introducing new lore.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yep, pretty much exactly that phrase was said ( typed) to me by Matthew Dawkins about V5 before it came out in an attempt to allay the concerns I had during playtesting.<br /> <br /> And here we are.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong, I'd super-love to be wrong but every recent experience I've had tells me I'm not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T10:59:34-08:00","id":1361931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361866#post1361866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;... a long time fan .........who says that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of ********** while introducing new lore.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Yep, pretty much exactly that phrase was said ( typed) to me by Matthew Dawkins about V5 before it came out in an attempt to allay the concerns I had during playtesting.<br /> <br /> And here we are.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm wrong, I'd super-love to be wrong but every recent experience I've had tells me I'm not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf does play differently from vampire as well. <br /> <br /> I was having a conversation with a long time vampire player about world of darkness and changed and he remarked \u201cthe world of today is not the world of the 90s.\u201d And taking that into account has made all the difference. <br /> <br /> For what it\u2019s worth I also hope you\u2019re wrong. We have at least one year to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T11:02:41-08:00","id":1361932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361860#post1361860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a longtime fan, were I to gain power over W5, I would drastically change a lot of things that have been getting under my skin for ages. A number of them are probably things that might not bother other people, or that others might actually have liked. Some of these might have even been central concepts; in my zeal to strike crossover from the integral structure of the game, for instance, I'd be at least sorely tempted to make drastic edits to the Silent Striders so that they spent too long around ghosts instead of being cursed by a borrowed, vampiric version of a Robert E. Howard character. I'm really tired of having to explain why the Metis breed is named the way it is in light of real world prejudices, and I'm not attached to the pseudeolatinate names of the others, so I would probably change them all, maybe even change the splat term &amp;quot;Breed&amp;quot; to something else like Birth, Origin, etc. Thrall of the Wyrm would be out (at least as a game term) in favor of Wits rolls for any frenzy to see if you chow down on a fallen enemy, like in 1e. If you're okay with Rage being measured in discrete states like the anima banner from Exalted 3rd edition, you wouldn't say that I boned it up, but if you were hoping for something closer to Hunger, well, it wouldn't be your lucky day if I ended up at the helm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elements of the game changing to modernize are not the same as boning up a central core of the game, and the things you suggested are not unreasonable. I think the bigger hang ups come from the depth of apocalypse lore, but changes are a thing and we\u2019ve accepted them before. He\u2019ll book of the wyrm 20 changed quite a bit about black spirals and for the better I feel. But the change is def easier in a game like forsaken where the stories are more left open as a possible reality, vs cWoD \u201cthis def happened.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T12:10:06-08:00","id":1361945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361839#post1361839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know where the hell you lot are deriving arrogance from on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I wouldn't call it arrogance exactly, it's mostly the part where you're trying to make us feel bad for not being excited about a product even though you've given us zero reasons to challenge our preconceptions based on experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The developer of w5 is a long time fan of werewolf who says (at least in the podcast) that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of werewolf while introducing new lore. It all sounded pretty good and frankly I\u2019m a little stoked. The whole crew dedicated themselves to getting this contract, and as fans I can\u2019t imagine they\u2019d want to bone it up. </div> </div> </div>This is what Martin, Kumar, and Matthew Dawkins have all said about V5. It might have gotten my intrigued back when V5 was still a plan and a pitch, but now that I've been burnt by the new WW on this, my ability to get stoked is rather dead.<br /> <br /> What has Ivan said that's supposed to reassure me that he's not going to repeat what happened with them? Hearing him talk, I'm hearing a lot of the same stuff we heard when Martin first started the rounds of promoting the new WW and V5.<br /> <br /> Also, the desire to not, &quot;bone it up,&quot; is also a problem. The nWoD/CofD is actually a great example here. The early nWoD books were too conservative in the desire to not bone it up, to make something new but familiar, and it ended up losing a lot of the cWoD fans instead of bringing them along. It wasn't until Changeling the Lost just going completely different from Dreaming that it became clear that the nWoD fans were cool with a much more unique game, and the cWoD fans that would be open to the nWoD definitely wanted more radical different takes on concepts. We saw this in how the CofD era lead to pushing the games much farther from their cWoD roots, and refining what makes them uniquely good games.<br /> <br /> You wouldn't get the CofD books now, by tossing the games to someone without the institutional memory and experience to accomplish that refinement. There's too many things that would look like insane risks to someone trying to not bone it up.<br /> <br /> Another example is the Exalted 3e development cycle and how messy the core book ended up because people were stepping up from making late-game supplements to being in-charge of the whole damned thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No what I\u2019ve seen from this thread is \u201cv5 is something I subjectively hate for x reason so w5 will be terrible because.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Dismissing it at, &quot;because,&quot; is no different than calling it lazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The podcast in question is the werewolf: the podcast. Give it a listen. </div> </div> </div>If you want people to listen to something? It helps to at least link to it. Most people aren't going to Goggle a podcast, dedicated 30 min. (or more for many) because you don't want to make a point for yourself.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://keepontheheathlands.podbean.com/e/werewolf-5th-edition-annoucement/\" target=\"_blank\">https://keepontheheathlands.podbean....n-annoucement/</a><br /> <br /> See? Not hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361931#post1361931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf does play differently from vampire as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't address the concerns being raised at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 01-19-2020, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T15:06:57-08:00","id":1361999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361866#post1361866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;... a long time fan .........who says that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of ********** while introducing new lore.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Yep, pretty much exactly that phrase was said ( typed) to me by Matthew Dawkins about V5 before it came out in an attempt to allay the concerns I had during playtesting.</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>And here we are.</b></u><br /> <br /> <b>Maybe I'm wrong</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Yes. Here we are. And I think you're wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Months later where V5 books led by Matthew Dawkins have made mucho $$$$$ on two Kickstarters and are both very favorably reviewed. Chicago by Night, from what I've been told, is amazing, and all of the previews from CotBG look fantastic. The last of which has just made 140k and broken past numerous stretch goals. These forums are SUPER negative when it comes to most things V5, and I understand why V5 devs wouldn't want to come here. I also understand that V5 is not for me, and that's cool, too. I love saving money. But I'd be an idiot to think it hasn't been successful--especially with Dawkins at the helm of Chicago by Night and Blood Gods.<br /> <br /> He HAS respected the World of Darkness, he has introduced new lore, and he IS a long-time fan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm willing to give W5 a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-19-2020, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T16:11:17-08:00","id":1362008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361999#post1361999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Yes. Here we are. And I think you're wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Months later where V5 books led by Matthew Dawkins have made mucho $$$$$ on two Kickstarters and are both very favorably reviewed. Chicago by Night, from what I've been told, is amazing, and all of the previews from CotBG look fantastic. The last of which has just made 140k and broken past numerous stretch goals. These forums are SUPER negative when it comes to most things V5, and I understand why V5 devs wouldn't want to come here. I also understand that V5 is not for me, and that's cool, too. I love saving money. But I'd be an idiot to think it hasn't been successful--especially with Dawkins at the helm of Chicago by Night and Blood Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Money doesn't enter into it. D&amp;D can easily make more money than all the WoD games combined, but there's a good reason that very few people are in a rush to make the WoD games more like D&amp;D. It would ruin the play style, clash with a lot of messages, and all around make a mess of things, particularly since a lot of people go into WW's rps because they weren't D&amp;D. That's setting aside that there are some things you can't just duplicate with design decisions, like the lengthy publishing history (17 years longer than V:tM as the Xerox of ttrpgs) or being owned and backed by Hasbro (ten times or more the worth of Paradox Entertainment AB, with much more influential IPs from board games).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He HAS respected the World of Darkness, he has introduced new lore, and he IS a long-time fan. </div> </div> </div>That's a question of personal taste. As noted in this thread several times, it's not really indicative of anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm willing to give W5 a chance. </div> </div> </div>To not be for you anymore, by your own admission?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T17:14:20-08:00","id":1362024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1362008#post1362008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Money doesn't enter into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I stopped reading after that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry.<br /> <br /> Take care.<br /> <br /> Edit: Sorry if that came off as harsh. But I have neither the energy nor time for something that would be so futile. IMO, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 01-19-2020, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T19:05:31-08:00","id":1362035,"title":"","content":"*Sigh*<br /> <br /> I think you missed my point.<br /> <br /> Long term fan. Check.<br /> Introduced New Lore. Check.<br /> Respectful to what has gone before. Probably in his own opinion, yes.<br /> <br /> And yet I've still ended up with a game that doesn't really resemble it's forebears very much at all and that, after trying it for an extended period of time, I've determined is basically unplayable for myself and others I have with.<br /> <br /> So, therefore, I would obviously have grave concerns on what my favourite game of the past 20+ years is going to be turned into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T19:10:27-08:00","id":1362037,"title":"","content":"I'm kinda also not sure why ' financially successful' was a metric you used as my post wasn't even referencing that aspect.<br /> <br /> OPP, to my recollection, always has successful kickstarters that is certainly not something I'd deny. ( After all, I backed a hell of a lot of them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T19:19:17-08:00","id":1362039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1362035#post1362035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Sigh*<br /> <br /> I think you missed my point.<br /> <br /> Long term fan. Check.<br /> Introduced New Lore. Check.<br /> Respectful to what has gone before. Probably in his own opinion, yes.<br /> <br /> And yet I've still ended up with a game that doesn't really resemble it's forebears very much at all and that, after trying it for an extended period of time, I've determined is basically unplayable for myself and others I have with.<br /> <br /> So, therefore, I would obviously have grave concerns on what my favourite game of the past 20+ years is going to be turned into.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nah. Didn't miss it.<br /> <br /> Was likely a bit too aggressive in my response as I've needed sleep that just continues to escape me.<br /> <br /> I apologize.<br /> <br /> I also realize that my comments were pretty asinine as I, too, am not a fan of V5. But I AM willing to give W5 a try since it happens to by one of my favorite RPGs, and I do like what was done with the last couple of V5 books. Though I guess that doesn't matter to much as they will be completely different creative teams.<br /> <br /> Who knows...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T19:40:56-08:00","id":1362040,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T08:57:49-08:00","id":1362125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361839#post1361839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t know where the hell you lot are deriving arrogance from on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never accused you of arrogance. I accused you of lumping all forms of criticism together as &quot;lazy and fearmongering&quot;, which I extrapolated from your statement of lumping all criticism together as lazy and fearmongering. I'd say it's a pretty valid accusation, all things considered.<br /> <br /> You can feel bad for the new devs because a subsection of fans are wary at best due to past products. But you can't expect a quote like...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1361839#post1361839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The developer of w5 is a long time fan of werewolf who says (at least in the podcast) that he\u2019s dedicated to respecting the world of werewolf while introducing new lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>...To change anything or anyone's mind, when almost the exact same quotes were used during V5's development. Or DnD4e's development. Or really any gameline with a revision that wasn't well recieved.<br /> <br /> Sometimes &quot;being a fan&quot; doesn't mean being capable of respecting what came before. I'm a Star Wars fan. I should not be trusted to make a good Star Wars movie. I'm a Spider-Man fan. I'd probably write the worst Spider-Man comic of all time. &quot;Being a fan&quot; is not a guarantee of quality by any single measure. It is not a valid qualifier to one's capabilities to continue a gameline, movie series, comic book or any form of media.<br /> <br /> But a good qualifier is past work. If I had to pick between Joss Whedon and Michael Bay for the next Star Wars movie, I'd pick Joss Whedon because I can base my expectations on both of their prior work. If I had to choose between Donny Cates and Tom King for the next Spider-Man comic? Donny Cates all the way, based on past work.<br /> <br /> So when I'm looking at past work, and I'm seeing things I don't like? I can pretty much rest assured I won't like the new product. It's not an unfair assumption; it's an informed one.<br /> <br /> I don't like V5. I don't like it from a narrative perspective, nor from a mechanical one. I haven't liked the post-core book products, nor did I like the direction of V20 products after nWW took over. Since nWW will still have a heavy hand in W5's development, I can make an informed assumption that just like a Michael Bay Star Wars movie or a Tom King Spider-Man comic, I won't like an nWW-directed or produced W5 game.<br /> <br /> So again, I'm not accusing you of arrogance, nor do I know where you're getting that assumption from. I'm definitely accusing you of ignoring the validity of all criticism in favor of your own opinion, which is simple short-sightedness. I'm accusing you of being short sighted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T10:30:24-07:00","id":1379491,"title":"","content":"Latest news:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hunters_ent/status/1247918255508869120?s=21\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/EVF9IpJVAAEPDkT?format=webp&amp;name=large\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hunters_ent/status/1247918255508869120?s=21\" target=\"_blank\"> Hunters Entertainment (@Hunters_Ent) on X </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/hunters_ent/status/1247918255508869120?s=21\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/hunters_ent/status/1247918255508869120?s=21 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Meet some of our amazing writers and development team on #Werewolf: The Apocalypse, discussing what drew them to contribute to the project: https://t.co/r03qA1z3Ha #werewolfRPG #w5e #worldofdarkness </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/Werewolf-The-Apocalypse---5th-Edition#click=https://t.co/r03qA1z3Ha\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://static.wixstatic.com/media/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png/v1/fill/w_2000,h_1125,al_c,q_95,usm_0.66_1.00_0.01/3e98ae_34d1c47c223d4d65940db5a3de149321~mv2.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/Werewolf-The-Apocalypse---5th-Edition#click=https://t.co/r03qA1z3Ha\" target=\"_blank\"> Werewolf: The Apocalypse - 5th Edition </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/Werewolf-The-Apocalypse---5th-Edition#click=https://t.co/r03qA1z3Ha\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.huntersentertainment.com/single-post/2020/04/08/Werewolf-The-Apocalypse---5th-Edition#click=https://t.co/r03qA1z3Ha </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A Storytelling Game of Savage Resistance Have you ever taken a moment to just stop, observe the world around you, and see the injustice of it all? You can see it, the scars and sores of the land. You can smell it, the degradation and decay in the air. You can feel it, the fever and tremors of a dying world. The question is: When will you rage? At its heart, Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a Storytelling game of Savage Resistance. What does that mean? It means that Werewolf: The Apocalypse is a gam </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T12:32:31-07:00","id":1379513,"title":"","content":"Really excited by this news!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T18:05:54-07:00","id":1379561,"title":"","content":"This was good news. Happy with the writing team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T18:50:52-07:00","id":1379568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1379561#post1379561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was good news. Happy with the writing team.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm 90% happy with the team, which is 40% more than I expected to be. Sambrano and Walters especially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:19:04-07:00","id":1379649,"title":"","content":"Seriously, Im really frustrated with all those comments. Why this fanbase need to be so pessimistic (and this is taking it kindly, what i've seen is basically full on hating) about every new installment of their beloved RPG?<br /> <br /> Times change, it's foolish to think a IP will not try to renew itself to attract new players, and Im not talking only about RPGs, movies, series, books, games, everything needs to make some effort to appear new and inviting for begginers. Cause the same old geezers will not be alive forever for sustain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hating on W5 cause &quot;V5 sucks&quot; is absolute bullshit, do they have the same writers? At least wait for it to be made (ot at least more news to be out) before you begin shitting on it.<br /> <br /> Cause even if W5 becomes a absolute steaming pile of shit everyone will still have W20 and everything that was made before. If you want the same old thing W20 will always be there.<br /> <br /> &quot;bUt WhY noT MakE a NEw WerewOLf GaMe?!?&quot;<br /> This IS a new game godammit. Old werewolf will always exist as W20 and older lines, this is a new werewolf game. And don't tell me about &quot;actual new game&quot; cause Im sure most people shitting on W5 also shat on them making forsaken cause they wanted to try something new without changing WTA.<br /> <br /> <br /> My personal opnion is that from all splats WtA is the one who can enjoy best and suffer less with dramatic changes to metaplot.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:38:13-07:00","id":1379688,"title":"","content":"Same as above. I had good feelings about the Hunrt and it seems that the company took good direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:00:23-07:00","id":1379786,"title":"","content":"As along as I don't have to wait too long for a Fera book, or books, I'm willing to give this edition a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T10:33:34-07:00","id":1379800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1379649#post1379649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, Im really frustrated with all those comments. Why this fanbase need to be so pessimistic (and this is taking it kindly, what i've seen is basically full on hating) about every new installment of their beloved RPG?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were concise run-downs about why just a few posts above.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Times change, it's foolish to think a IP will not try to renew itself to attract new players, and Im not talking only about RPGs, movies, series, books, games, everything needs to make some effort to appear new and inviting for begginers. Cause the same old geezers will not be alive forever for sustain it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hating on W5 cause &quot;V5 sucks&quot; is absolute bullshit, do they have the same writers? At least wait for it to be made (ot at least more news to be out) before you begin shitting on it.<br /> <br /> Cause even if W5 becomes a absolute steaming pile of shit everyone will still have W20 and everything that was made before. If you want the same old thing W20 will always be there.<br /> <br /> &quot;bUt WhY noT MakE a NEw WerewOLf GaMe?!?&quot;<br /> This IS a new game godammit. Old werewolf will always exist as W20 and older lines, this is a new werewolf game. And don't tell me about &quot;actual new game&quot; cause Im sure most people shitting on W5 also shat on them making forsaken cause they wanted to try something new without changing WTA. </div> </div> </div>Forsaken has been compared to playing INS for spirits, so if one was accustomed to a punk atmosphere for Werewolf, then, uh, it's sort of natural that they might not like Forsaken that much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My personal opnion is that from all splats WtA is the one who can enjoy best and suffer less with dramatic changes to metaplot. </div> </div> </div>A set of changes to which we, the public, are not privy to in their entirety, and which we can only go on based on Changing Ways. Another inspiration for pessimism, that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:30:16-07:00","id":1379862,"title":"","content":"I for one am looking forward to the new game and if I don't like already understand that I can just play W20. There is nothing wrong with that. I'll have a game no matter what. so I hope hunters the best and look forward to seeing what they do with the setting.<br /> <br /> If it upsets you Runcun, know that there is a non vocal minority that supports things and just don't listen to the hate, as hard as that might be. for one if you want to join the convo over on the hunters discord there is positive things going on there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T02:41:32-07:00","id":1380065,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ok after looking over the information HE have released so far I have some questions:</span></span></span><ul><li>What is &quot; The Malady&quot;? ( if its basically The Beckoning but for Werewolves I'm gonna throatpunch someone......)</li> <li>The Gauntlet Hardening ( So I guess we're going Weaver Ascendant.....which makes less sense now than in the 90s but I can live with it)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Edit: Tracked it down....of all fucking books to reference *gag* Changing Ways. I guess we know why NuWhite Wolf went so hard on the hatchet job they did to that book. They were laying the foundations for W5....<br /> <br /> Harder to step sideways, spiritscapes at all Caerns are corrupted and hostile......urgh.....Basically Avatar Storm but for WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-10-2020, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:26:59-07:00","id":1380107,"title":"","content":"The malady was mentioned in w20 the changing ways in a sidebar called Future Fates.<br /> <br /> It only has a small section but basically it is about Gia dying and drawing further away from the world to protect herself. The mechanics in W20 was that the Gaunlet goes up by 4 and nothing can cross the Gauntlet if it is 9 or higher. Basically meaning that you can not cross unless you are in the woods, veranda or other special spot that would have a seeker Gauntlet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:59:42-07:00","id":1380116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1353412#post1353412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If it was the mechanics of V5 that is what you don\u2019t like, then it is probably a safe assumption to think you won\u2019t like W5 since they have already announced that it will use similar mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I accept that not everyone will like W5; I think fans get settled into their preferred edition, which is cool; what really matters is that you play whatever edition you like to tell stories; V5 is what brought me back to VtM after Revised; if W5 is anything like V5 then Im sold. Im really excited for the writing and development team; that alone will make me pick up W5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/337-joe","name":"Joe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:01:10-07:00","id":1380117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1379568#post1379568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm 90% happy with the team, which is 40% more than I expected to be. Sambrano and Walters especially.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, when I saw Sambrano, Walters and Dawkins, I was sold!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/337-joe","name":"Joe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar337_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:23:25-07:00","id":1380127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380117#post1380117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep, when I saw Sambrano, Walters and Dawkins, I was sold!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I'm so glad we have such a talented, diverse team.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T08:40:56-07:00","id":1380133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380107#post1380107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The malady was mentioned in w20 the changing ways in a sidebar called Future Fates.<br /> <br /> It only has a small section but basically it is about Gia dying and drawing further away from the world to protect herself. The mechanics in W20 was that the Gaunlet goes up by 4 and nothing can cross the Gauntlet if it is 9 or higher. Basically meaning that you can not cross unless you are in the woods, veranda or other special spot that would have a seeker Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you can\u2019t create a level 5 caern unless invest 100 gnosis, man<br /> <br /> W20 is even worse than Revised. The Middle Kingdom has been filled with Black Spiral Dancers (in Book of Wyrm 2nd edition they are few)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:28:12-07:00","id":1380163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380116#post1380116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I accept that not everyone will like W5; I think fans get settled into their preferred edition, which is cool; what really matters is that you play whatever edition you like to tell stories; V5 is what brought me back to VtM after Revised; if W5 is anything like V5 then Im sold. Im really excited for the writing and development team; that alone will make me pick up W5.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Could not agree more.<br /> <br /> It is really cool to me how we have access to so many editions of the game and can just take for others what we want and leave the rest.<br /> <br /> Personally I am all in board for 5th in Vampire I am hoping the same for W5. And am resting assured with this team that I will not be disappointed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 04-10-2020, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:30:57-07:00","id":1380164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380065#post1380065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Ok after looking over the information HE have released so far I have some questions:</span></span></span><ul><li>What is &quot; The Malady&quot;? ( if its basically The Beckoning but for Werewolves I'm gonna throatpunch someone......)</li> <li>The Gauntlet Hardening ( So I guess we're going Weaver Ascendant.....which makes less sense now than in the 90s but I can live with it)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Edit: Tracked it down....of all fucking books to reference *gag* Changing Ways. I guess we know why NuWhite Wolf went so hard on the hatchet job they did to that book. They were laying the foundations for W5....<br /> <br /> Harder to step sideways, spiritscapes at all Caerns are corrupted and hostile......urgh.....Basically Avatar Storm but for WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of the Avatar Storm, it was retconned into having partially applied to Garou and Fera in the same book. In spite of the fact that they don't have Avatars or work the way Mage does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:12:25-07:00","id":1380190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380116#post1380116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...what really matters is that you play whatever edition you like to tell stories;</div> </div> </div> </div>It would really help if people stop with this thing.<br /> <br /> You know why?<br /> <br /> Basically every WoD gameline besides V20 is either incomplete or in some cases non-existent. After nWW shat on W20, we've got not equivalent of Lore of the Clans for the Tribes, nothing like M20 Book of Secrets to collect a lot of expanded customization options that didn't make it into the core book, etc. Changeling, and Wraith are similarly not getting a chance for a decent catalog of 20th supplements. We don't have a Numina20th book to cover WoD: Sorcerer or Sorcerer Revised, just a few Numina scattered across a few books. Mummy, Hunter, Demon, and (yet controversial but the point stands) Kindred of the East aren't getting 20th books at all.<br /> <br /> Yes, there's the Storyteller Vault where a lot of freelancers are putting what probably would have been those supplements, but a lot of us don't play in groups that allow &quot;unofficial&quot; material or don't do so lightly (more now than ever with more gaming moving online with COVID-19).<br /> <br /> If WW committed to letting Onyx Path finish the 20th lines, and not repeating the off-putting use of editorial oversight we saw in Shattering Dreams and Changing Ways? It'd be a lot easier to accept the &quot;W5 isn't my jam, but I have W20.&quot; Since 20th got canned for 5th before a lot of books could get made, this sentiment is going to create division no matter how much it's meant to be a call to unity and understanding... because it completely lacks in understanding.<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> I will say, the writing team is a good one. I stand by my previous worries about the lack of WtA professional experience there (esp. with lots of non-Hunters Entertainment or Renegade people working on it ), but if nothing else I'm confident that W5 is going to be written way better than V5 was.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:23:09-07:00","id":1380216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380164#post1380164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of the Avatar Storm, it was retconned into having partially applied to Garou and Fera in the same book. In spite of the fact that they don't have Avatars or work the way Mage does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup. I mean....yeah....why lean on the book that is the worst example of corporate interference in artistic endeavour of the entire line?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:26:41-07:00","id":1380217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1353351-hunters-entertainment-with-paradox-to-create-werewolf-the-apocalypse-5th-edition?p=1380107#post1380107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The malady was mentioned in w20 the changing ways in a sidebar called Future Fates.<br /> <br /> It only has a small section but basically it is about Gia dying and drawing further away from the world to protect herself. The mechanics in W20 was that the Gaunlet goes up by 4 and nothing can cross the Gauntlet if it is 9 or higher. Basically meaning that you